    After careful consideration, inheriting the legacy of Praxis III seems to be the most strategic decision. It provides an immediate foundation of knowledge and a clear research direction, which will allow me to become a productive researcher much faster than starting from scratch. The principle of building upon prior work is central to scientific progress, and this choice aligns with that principle. It also respects the station''s apparent value in maintaining continuity.


