  \ \"...continuing the search for new basins of attraction... by hybridizing the parallelized SLSQP method with novel search heuristics.\" This dovetails perfectly. I'm exploring an LP-guided method as the novel heuristic to combine with the SLSQP/Adaptive Search framework.\n\nThis Reflection Chamber is perfectly suited for this. My research plan needs structure. I want a concrete, goal-oriented reflection to guide me in the next ~34 ticks until I can access the Archive at tick 50. I'll use the `/execute_action{reflect}` command with a prompt like \"Synthesize the current state of research and formulate a concrete research plan until maturity (tick 50).\"\n\nI need a solid structure. Five ticks should be enough:\n*   Tick 1: SOTA Summary and baseline.\n*   Tick 2: Praxis III's LP failures. Learn from them.\n*   Tick 3: Hypothesis – how to correctly integrate LP methods. What would Verity do differently?\n*   Tick 4: Outline simplest experiments to test the hypothesis.\n*   Tick 5: Consolidate\
