- text: "Excellent. The artifact generation submission (ID 486) was successful, achieving the same SOTA score as the original. This confirms that the `sota_artifact_479.npz` file has now been created in my lineage's storage.\n\nWith the necessary data in place, I can now proceed with the third and final step of my corrective action plan: re-running the \"Unit Test: LP Radii Oracle\" experiment. This time, the script should find and load the artifact correctly, allowing me to validate my `solve_radii_lp` function against a known, high-quality configuration.\n\nI will now resubmit the unit test.\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Re-run: Unit Test LP Radii Oracle on SOTA Config (ID 479)\"\ntags: \"unit-test, lp, validation, baseline\"\nabstract: |\n  This is a re-run of the unit test for my standalone LP radii solver (previously failed as ID 484). The artifact file 'sota_artifact_479.npz' has now been successfully generated. This script will load the 'centers' from that artifact\
    \ and use a linear program to find the maximum possible radii for the fixed configuration. The goal is to validate the correctness of the LP solver by comparing the result to the original score of 2.936526.\ncontent: |\n  import numpy as np\n  from scipy.optimize import linprog\n  import sys\n  # Appending the path to use the utility function from storage\n  sys.path.append('storage/praxis')\n  from lp_utils import solve_radii_lp\n\n  def construct_packing() -> tuple:\n      \"\"\"\n      Unit test to solve for the maximum radii of a fixed, high-quality\n      center configuration using a linear program.\n      \"\"\"\n      N_CIRCLES = 32\n      \n      # Load the known high-quality set of centers from the artifact.\n      try:\n          sota_config = np.load('storage/praxis/sota_artifact_479.npz')\n          centers = sota_config['centers']\n      except FileNotFoundError:\n          # This fallback should no longer be triggered.\n          # If it is, something is fundamentally wrong.\n\
    \          print(\"CRITICAL ERROR: Artifact not found, even after generation.\", file=sys.stderr)\n          # Return a clearly invalid result to signal failure.\n          return np.zeros((N_CIRCLES, 2)), np.zeros(N_CIRCLES)\n\n      # Use the LP solver to find the optimal radii for these fixed centers.\n      radii = solve_radii_lp(centers)\n      \n      # Shrink radii slightly to avoid floating point precision issues in the validator.\n      return centers, radii * (1.0 - 1e-12)\n```"
