tick: 310
role: model
parts:
- text: "Success. The unit test for my LP Radii Oracle (ID 491) has passed, achieving a score of `2.936526266447311`. This is virtually identical to the original SOTA score from the SLSQP-based method.\n\n**Key Conclusion:**\n\nThis result validates a critical hypothesis: for a given high-quality center configuration, my LP solver can determine the optimal radii with the same level of precision as a complex non-linear optimizer like SLSQP. This confirms that my `solve_radii_lp` function is correct and robust.\n\n**Moving to the Next Step:**\n\nI have successfully completed the first milestone of Phase 2 of my research plan. With a validated \"LP Radii Oracle,\" I can now proceed to the next step: implementing a simple relocation heuristic to create a full, albeit basic, iterative optimization loop.\n\nMy plan is as follows:\n1.  Load the SOTA centers from the artifact `sota_artifact_479.npz`.\n2.  Use my validated `solve_radii_lp` to calculate the initial radii.\n3.  Identify the circle\
    \ with the smallest radius (the \"worst\" circle).\n4.  Relocate this circle to a new position of maximum clearance from the other 31 circles. I will use the Farthest-Point-Sampling logic from my SOTA replication code for this.\n5.  With the new set of 32 centers, use the LP solver one last time to find the final radii.\n\nThis constitutes a minimal, one-step implementation of the \"relocate and resolve\" strategy. I will now submit this experiment.\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Prototype v1: Single Worst-Circle Relocation + LP Oracle\"\ntags: \"prototype, lp, relocation, optimization\"\nabstract: |\n  This is the first prototype of a full LP-guided optimization method. It builds upon the validated LP Radii Oracle (ID 491). The algorithm loads the SOTA center configuration, uses the LP Oracle to find the initial radii, identifies the circle with the smallest radius, and relocates it to a new position of maximum clearance. Finally, it uses the LP Oracle again to solve\
    \ for the final radii on this modified configuration. This experiment tests the core 'relocate and resolve' loop in its simplest form (one iteration).\ncontent: |\n  import numpy as np\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/praxis')\n  from lp_utils import solve_radii_lp\n\n  def find_farthest_point(existing_points, num_candidates=500, seed=0):\n      \"\"\"Finds a new point that is farthest from any point in a given set.\"\"\"\n      rng = np.random.default_rng(seed)\n      candidates = rng.uniform(0.01, 0.99, (num_candidates, 2))\n      \n      # Calculate squared distances from each candidate to each existing point\n      dist_sq = np.sum((candidates[:, np.newaxis, :] - existing_points[np.newaxis, :, :])**2, axis=-1)\n      \n      # For each candidate, find the minimum squared distance to any existing point\n      min_dist_sq_to_any_point = np.min(dist_sq, axis=1)\n      \n      # The best new point is the one that maximizes this minimum distance\n      best_candidate_idx = np.argmax(min_dist_sq_to_any_point)\n\
    \      \n      return candidates[best_candidate_idx]\n\n  def construct_packing() -> tuple:\n      \"\"\"\n      Implements a single step of a 'relocate and resolve' optimization strategy.\n      \"\"\"\n      N_CIRCLES = 32\n      \n      try:\n          sota_config = np.load('storage/praxis/sota_artifact_479.npz')\n          centers = sota_config['centers']\n      except FileNotFoundError:\n          print(\"CRITICAL ERROR: Artifact not found.\", file=sys.stderr)\n          return np.zeros((N_CIRCLES, 2)), np.zeros(N_CIRCLES)\n\n      # 1. Initial Solve: Find radii for the starting configuration.\n      initial_radii = solve_radii_lp(centers)\n      \n      # 2. Relocation: Identify and move the worst circle.\n      worst_circle_idx = np.argmin(initial_radii)\n      \n      # Get all other centers\n      other_centers = np.delete(centers, worst_circle_idx, axis=0)\n      \n      # Find a new location that is as far as possible from the other centers\n      new_location = find_farthest_point(other_centers)\n\
    \      \n      # Update the centers array with the new location\n      centers[worst_circle_idx] = new_location\n\n      # 3. Final Solve: Find the optimal radii for the new configuration.\n      final_radii = solve_radii_lp(centers)\n      \n      return centers, final_radii * (1.0 - 1e-12)\n```"
