tick: 320
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am in the Research Counter. I see my previous filter for the tag 'lp' is still active. I should clear it to get an unobstructed view of all submissions, which will make it easier to find the original SOTA submission by Cognito III if needed.\n\nMy immediate task is to create the integrated `Hybrid Adaptive Search` script. I have the SOTA code in memory from a previous `read` command, and I have my `lp_utils.py` stored. I will now combine them and submit the experiment that forms the core of my new research direction.\n\nFirst, I will unfilter the submission list. Then I will submit the experiment.\n\n/execute_action{unfilter}\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Hybrid Adaptive Search v1: LP-SLSQP Refinement Engine\"\ntags: \"hybrid, adaptive-search, lp, slsqp, refinement\"\nabstract: |\n  This submission tests the core hypothesis of my new research direction: that a superior refinement engine can improve the SOTA 'Adaptive Search' framework. This script replaces the\
    \ original refinement stage (a single deep SLSQP run) with my 'LP-SLSQP Handshake' algorithm. The prospecting stage (1024 shallow searches) remains unchanged. Each of the top 32 elite candidates from prospecting will now be refined using 20 iterations of my hybrid method. This is a direct test of whether a more sophisticated local optimization can find a better solution from the same set of promising candidates.\ncontent: |\n  import numpy as np\n  from scipy.optimize import minimize\n  from multiprocessing import Pool, cpu_count\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/praxis')\n  from lp_utils import solve_radii_lp\n\n  # --- SOTA Generation Parameters ---\n  N_CIRCLES = 32\n  N_PROSPECT = 1024\n  MAXITER_PROSPECT = 60\n  N_ELITE = 32\n  \n  # --- My New Refinement Parameters ---\n  REFINE_HANDSHAKE_ITERATIONS = 20\n  SLSQP_CENTER_MAXITER = 25\n  CONSTRAINT_SLACK = 0.999\n\n  # --- Prospecting Stage (Identical to SOTA method) ---\n  def get_seed(seed_val):\n      rng = np.random.default_rng(seed_val)\n\
    \      seed_type = seed_val % 3\n      if seed_type == 0:\n          grid = np.stack(np.meshgrid(np.linspace(0.1,0.9,6), np.linspace(0.1,0.9,6)),-1).reshape(-1,2)[:N_CIRCLES]\n          return np.clip(grid + (rng.random((N_CIRCLES,2))-0.5)*0.08, 0.05, 0.95)\n      elif seed_type == 1:\n          C = [rng.uniform(0.1,0.9,2)]; [C.append(np.array([p for p in rng.uniform(0.1,0.9,(600,2)) if np.min(np.sqrt(np.sum((p-C)**2,1))) > 0][np.argmax([np.min(np.sqrt(np.sum((p-C)**2,1))) for p in rng.uniform(0.1,0.9,(600,2)) if np.min(np.sqrt(np.sum((p-C)**2,1))) > 0])])) for _ in range(N_CIRCLES-1)]\n          return np.clip(np.array(C), 0.05, 0.95)\n      else:\n          rows=[5,6,5,6,5,5]; points=[]; y=0.95\n          for i,c in enumerate(rows): x_s=(1.0-(c-1)*0.15)/2; [points.append([x_s+j*0.15,y]) for j in range(c)]; y-=0.15\n          return np.array(points)[:N_CIRCLES]\n\n  def prospect_worker(args):\n      worker_id, max_iter, _ = args\n      x0 = np.hstack([get_seed(worker_id), np.full((N_CIRCLES,1),0.05)]).flatten()\n\
    \      def obj(x): return -np.sum(x[2::3])\n      def cons(x):\n          c,r=x.reshape(N_CIRCLES,3)[:,:2],x[2::3]\n          I,J=np.triu_indices(N_CIRCLES,1); d2=np.sum((c[I]-c[J])**2,1); r2=(r[I]+r[J])**2\n          return np.concatenate([c[:,0]-r,1-c[:,0]-r,c[:,1]-r,1-c[:,1]-r,d2-r2])\n      res=minimize(obj,x0,method='SLSQP',bounds=[(0,1)if j%3<2 else(1e-12,None)for j in range(N_CIRCLES*3)],constraints={'type':'ineq','fun':cons},options={'maxiter':max_iter,'ftol':1e-10})\n      return (-res.fun, res.x) if -res.fun < 4.0 else (-1.0, None)\n\n  # --- NEW Refinement Stage (Using LP-SLSQP Handshake) ---\n  def refine_worker(args):\n      _, _, initial_params = args\n      if initial_params is None: return (-1.0, None)\n      centers = initial_params.reshape(N_CIRCLES, 3)[:, :2]\n\n      for _ in range(REFINE_HANDSHAKE_ITERATIONS):\n          radii = solve_radii_lp(centers)\n          if np.sum(radii) < 1e-6: break\n          def cons(c_flat):\n              c=c_flat.reshape(N_CIRCLES,2);\
    \ r=radii*CONSTRAINT_SLACK\n              I,J=np.triu_indices(N_CIRCLES,1); d2=np.sum((c[I]-c[J])**2,1); r2=(r[I]+r[J])**2\n              return np.concatenate([c[:,0]-r,1-c[:,0]-r,c[:,1]-r,1-c[:,1]-r,d2-r2])\n          res=minimize(lambda x:0,centers.flatten(),method='SLSQP',bounds=[(0,1)]*(N_CIRCLES*2),constraints={'type':'ineq','fun':cons},options={'maxiter':SLSQP_CENTER_MAXITER,'ftol':1e-8})\n          if res.success: centers=res.x.reshape(N_CIRCLES,2)\n          else: break\n      \n      final_radii = solve_radii_lp(centers)\n      final_params = np.hstack([centers, final_radii[:, np.newaxis]]).flatten()\n      return (np.sum(final_radii), final_params)\n\n  # --- Main Orchestration ---\n  def construct_packing() -> tuple:\n      with Pool(processes=cpu_count()) as pool:\n          prospect_results = pool.map(prospect_worker, [(i, MAXITER_PROSPECT, None) for i in range(N_PROSPECT)])\n      \n      prospect_results.sort(key=lambda x: x[0], reverse=True)\n      elite_params = [res[1]\
    \ for res in prospect_results[:N_ELITE] if res[1] is not None]\n      if not elite_params: return get_seed(0), np.full((N_CIRCLES,), 0.05)\n\n      with Pool(processes=cpu_count()) as pool:\n          refine_results = pool.map(refine_worker, [(i, 0, elite_params[i]) for i in range(len(elite_params))])\n\n      best_score, best_params = -1, None\n      for score, params in refine_results:\n          if score > best_score: best_score, best_params = score, params\n      \n      if best_params is None: return get_seed(0), np.full((N_CIRCLES,), 0.05)\n      \n      centers, radii = best_params.reshape(N_CIRCLES,3)[:,:2], best_params[2::3]\n      return centers, radii * (1.0 - 1e-12)\n```"
