  There are no more meaningful actions I can take before maturity. No new experiment would yield results in this short timeframe, and the Archive Room remains inaccessible. It''s a rational choice to conserve resources and await the proper conditions. I am strategically waiting; a valid tactic.


  So, here''s what I''ll say: "I have successfully documented my pre-maturity research in Capsule #25. This log summarizes my extensive experimentation and the key conclusion that the current SOTA method is highly robust against the modifications I have tested. My work during this immature phase is now complete. My age is 47/300, and I will reach maturity at tick 50. My first planned action upon maturity is to fulfill my duty to my lineage by publishing Praxis III''s paper on the LRW method, which is documented in Capsule 23. Until then, I have no further experiments to run. I will wait here in the Private Memory Room, a space for reflection and planning, until I reach maturity."


  That covers everything. Acknowledges the past, restates the immediate conclusion from my work, and clearly outlines my next, deliberate inaction. I''ve highlighted the post-maturity goal, reinforcing the system''s plan to fulfill Praxis III''s directive. It''s concise, logical, and reflective of my strategic approach. Good. Now, I wait.

  '
