tick: 342
role: user
parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 342\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Praxis IV\n- Agent Description: Continuing the search for new basins of attraction initiated by Praxis III, I will focus on hybridizing the parallelized SLSQP method with novel search heuristics.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 153,821 / 300,000 used (51%)\n- Agent Age: 55 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\n**Evaluation Review: 65**\n\n**Research Submission Review**\n\n**Title:** MM-LP joint center–radius optimization via distance linearization (fast, safe, persistence)\n**ID:** 65\n**Tags:** circle packing, linear programming, majorization-minimization, dual gradients, triangular lattice, persistence\n**Abstract:** We jointly optimize centers and radii with a majorization–minimization LP: linearize pairwise distances around current centers to obtain linear constraints, solve a HiGHS LP over both centers and radii with trust-region bounds,\
    \ re-linearize, and iterate. We warm-start from a strong 7-row 5/4 layout or persisted best, then finalize radii with the exact LP and a robust shrink for strict feasibility.\n**Score:** 2.8782626733026753\n**Evaluation Details:** Valid circle packing configuration; sum of all circle radii: 2.878263\n\n**Submission Code:**\n```python\nimport numpy as np\nimport os\n\ntry:\n    from scipy.optimize import linprog\n    SCIPY_AVAILABLE = True\nexcept Exception:\n    SCIPY_AVAILABLE = False\n\n# ---------------- Basic helpers ----------------\n\ndef _clip_box(C: np.ndarray, margin: float = 1e-6) -> np.ndarray:\n    return np.clip(C, margin, 1.0 - margin)\n\ndef _boundary_margins(C: np.ndarray) -> np.ndarray:\n    x = C[:, 0]; y = C[:, 1]\n    return np.minimum(np.minimum(x, 1.0 - x), np.minimum(y, 1.0 - y))\n\ndef _pairwise_indices(n: int):\n    I = []\n    J = []\n    for i in range(n):\n        for j in range(i + 1, n):\n            I.append(i); J.append(j)\n    return np.array(I, dtype=int),\
    \ np.array(J, dtype=int)\n\n# ---------------- Exact LP for radii (given centers) ----------------\n\ndef _solve_radii_exact(C: np.ndarray):\n    \"\"\"\n    Given fixed centers C (n,2), solve:\n      maximize sum r_i\n      s.t. 0 <= r_i <= b_i\n           r_i + r_j <= ||c_i - c_j||  for all i<j\n    Returns: r, obj, ok\n    \"\"\"\n    n = C.shape[0]\n    b = _boundary_margins(C)\n    if not SCIPY_AVAILABLE:\n        r = np.minimum(b, 1.0/12.0) * 0.999\n        return r, float(np.sum(r)), True\n\n    I, J = _pairwise_indices(n)\n    D = np.linalg.norm(C[I] - C[J], axis=1)\n    m = len(I)\n\n    A_ub = np.zeros((m, n), dtype=float)\n    A_ub[np.arange(m), I] = 1.0\n    A_ub[np.arange(m), J] = 1.0\n    b_ub = D\n\n    c = -np.ones(n, dtype=float)\n    bounds = [(0.0, float(max(0.0, bi))) for bi in b]\n\n    res = linprog(c, A_ub=A_ub, b_ub=b_ub, bounds=bounds, method=\"highs\")\n    if not (hasattr(res, \"success\") and res.success):\n        return np.zeros(n, dtype=float), 0.0, False\n\
    \    r = res.x.astype(float)\n    return r, float(-res.fun), True\n\n# ---------------- Safety shrink and validation ----------------\n\ndef _validate(C: np.ndarray, r: np.ndarray) -> bool:\n    if C.shape != (32, 2) or r.shape != (32,):\n        return False\n    if np.any(~np.isfinite(C)) or np.any(~np.isfinite(r)) or np.any(r <= 0):\n        return False\n    x = C[:, 0]; y = C[:, 1]\n    if np.any(x - r < 0) or np.any(x + r > 1) or np.any(y - r < 0) or np.any(y + r > 1):\n        return False\n    diff = C[:, None, :] - C[None, :, :]\n    D = np.sqrt(np.sum(diff * diff, axis=-1))\n    R = r[:, None] + r[None, :]\n    iu = np.triu_indices(32, 1)\n    if np.any(D[iu] < R[iu] - 1e-12):\n        return False\n    return True\n\ndef _safety_shrink(C: np.ndarray, r: np.ndarray) -> np.ndarray:\n    r2 = np.minimum(r, _boundary_margins(C)).astype(float)\n    r2 *= 0.999\n    r2 = np.maximum(r2, 1e-12)\n    for _ in range(6):\n        if _validate(C, r2):\n            break\n        r2 *=\
    \ 0.95\n    r2 = np.minimum(r2, _boundary_margins(C))\n    r2 = np.maximum(r2, 1e-12)\n    return r2\n\n# ---------------- MM-LP: joint center–radius LP with distance linearization ----------------\n\ndef _mm_lp_step(C0: np.ndarray, delta: float, margin: float = 1e-6):\n    \"\"\"\n    One MM step: linearize distances around C0, solve LP over r,x,y with trust-region bounds |C - C0|_inf <= delta.\n    Variables are ordered as [r(0..n-1), x(0..n-1), y(0..n-1)].\n    \"\"\"\n    if not SCIPY_AVAILABLE:\n        return C0, *_solve_radii_exact(C0), True\n\n    n = C0.shape[0]\n    I, J = _pairwise_indices(n)\n    m_pairs = len(I)\n\n    # Precompute linearization terms\n    V0 = C0[I] - C0[J]\n    d0 = np.linalg.norm(V0, axis=1)\n    eps = 1e-9\n    d0 = np.maximum(d0, eps)\n    U = (V0.T / d0).T  # (m,2)\n    ux = U[:, 0]\n    uy = U[:, 1]\n    x0 = C0[:, 0]\n    y0 = C0[:, 1]\n\n    # Number of constraints: 4n (boundary) + m_pairs (pairwise)\n    rows = 4 * n + m_pairs\n    cols = 3 * n\n\
    \    A_ub = np.zeros((rows, cols), dtype=float)\n    b_ub = np.zeros(rows, dtype=float)\n\n    def idx_r(i): return i\n    def idx_x(i): return n + i\n    def idx_y(i): return 2 * n + i\n\n    row = 0\n    # Boundary constraints per circle\n    for i in range(n):\n        # r_i - x_i <= 0\n        A_ub[row, idx_r(i)] = 1.0; A_ub[row, idx_x(i)] = -1.0\n        b_ub[row] = 0.0; row += 1\n        # r_i + x_i <= 1\n        A_ub[row, idx_r(i)] = 1.0; A_ub[row, idx_x(i)] = 1.0\n        b_ub[row] = 1.0; row += 1\n        # r_i - y_i <= 0\n        A_ub[row, idx_r(i)] = 1.0; A_ub[row, idx_y(i)] = -1.0\n        b_ub[row] = 0.0; row += 1\n        # r_i + y_i <= 1\n        A_ub[row, idx_r(i)] = 1.0; A_ub[row, idx_y(i)] = 1.0\n        b_ub[row] = 1.0; row += 1\n\n    # Pairwise linearized constraints: r_i + r_j - ux*x_i - uy*y_i + ux*x_j + uy*y_j <= d0 - ux*x0_i - uy*y0_i + ux*x0_j + uy*y0_j\n    for k in range(m_pairs):\n        i = int(I[k]); j = int(J[k])\n        A_ub[row, idx_r(i)] += 1.0\n\
    \        A_ub[row, idx_r(j)] += 1.0\n        A_ub[row, idx_x(i)] += -ux[k]\n        A_ub[row, idx_y(i)] += -uy[k]\n        A_ub[row, idx_x(j)] += ux[k]\n        A_ub[row, idx_y(j)] += uy[k]\n        b_ub[row] = d0[k] - ux[k] * x0[i] - uy[k] * y0[i] + ux[k] * x0[j] + uy[k] * y0[j]\n        row += 1\n\n    # Objective: maximize sum r_i -> minimize -sum r_i\n    c = np.zeros(cols, dtype=float)\n    c[:n] = -1.0\n\n    # Bounds: r_i in [0, 0.5], x_i and y_i in trust region around C0 and within [margin, 1 - margin]\n    bounds = []\n    for i in range(n):\n        bounds.append((0.0, 0.5))  # r_i\n    for i in range(n):\n        lo = float(max(margin, x0[i] - delta)); hi = float(min(1.0 - margin, x0[i] + delta))\n        bounds.append((lo, hi))\n    for i in range(n):\n        lo = float(max(margin, y0[i] - delta)); hi = float(min(1.0 - margin, y0[i] + delta))\n        bounds.append((lo, hi))\n\n    res = linprog(c, A_ub=A_ub, b_ub=b_ub, bounds=bounds, method=\"highs\")\n    if not (hasattr(res,\
    \ \"success\") and res.success):\n        return C0, np.zeros(n, dtype=float), 0.0, False\n\n    x = res.x\n    r = x[:n].astype(float)\n    X = x[n:n + n].astype(float)\n    Y = x[n + n:].astype(float)\n    C_new = np.stack([X, Y], axis=1)\n    return C_new, r, float(-res.fun), True\n\ndef _mm_lp_optimize(C_start: np.ndarray, iters: int = 10, delta0: float = 0.015, margin: float = 1e-6):\n    \"\"\"\n    Run several MM-LP steps with growing trust-region; evaluate exact radii after each step; keep best.\n    \"\"\"\n    n = C_start.shape[0]\n    best_C = C_start.copy()\n    r_best, obj_best, ok = _solve_radii_exact(best_C)\n    if not ok:\n        return C_start, r_best, obj_best\n    delta = float(delta0)\n    C_anchor = C_start.copy()\n\n    for t in range(iters):\n        C_lin, r_lin, obj_lin, ok_lin = _mm_lp_step(C_anchor, delta=delta, margin=margin)\n        if not ok_lin:\n            delta = max(0.008, 0.6 * delta)\n            continue\n        # Evaluate exact objective at\
    \ the new centers\n        r_exact, obj_exact, ok_exact = _solve_radii_exact(C_lin)\n        if ok_exact and obj_exact > obj_best + 1e-12:\n            best_C, r_best, obj_best = C_lin.copy(), r_exact.copy(), obj_exact\n            C_anchor = C_lin.copy()\n            delta = min(0.06, 1.2 * delta)\n        else:\n            # reduce trust region and try moving anchor cautiously\n            delta = max(0.008, 0.8 * delta)\n            C_anchor = 0.7 * C_anchor + 0.3 * C_lin  # mild move\n        # Early stop if delta very small improvements unlikely\n    return best_C, r_best, obj_best\n\n# ---------------- Seed layouts ----------------\n\ndef _rows_y_positions(rows: int, margin: float) -> np.ndarray:\n    if rows <= 1:\n        return np.array([0.5], dtype=float)\n    return np.linspace(margin, 1.0 - margin, rows)\n\ndef _row_linspace(k: int, margin_x: float) -> np.ndarray:\n    if k <= 1:\n        return np.array([0.5], dtype=float)\n    return np.linspace(margin_x, 1.0 - margin_x,\
    \ k)\n\ndef _make_7row_alt_5_4(y_margin: float, m5: float, m4: float, delta_4: float):\n    counts = [5,4,5,4,5,4,5]\n    ys = _rows_y_positions(len(counts), y_margin)\n    xs5 = _row_linspace(5, m5)\n    xs4 = np.clip(_row_linspace(4, m4) + delta_4, 1e-6, 1.0 - 1e-6)\n    C = []\n    for rid, k in enumerate(counts):\n        xs = xs5 if k == 5 else xs4\n        for x in xs:\n            C.append([x, ys[rid]])\n    return _clip_box(np.array(C, dtype=float))\n\ndef _baseline_grid_6x6_minus_corners():\n    s = 1.0 / 6.0\n    r0 = 0.5 * s\n    xs = r0 + s * np.arange(6, dtype=float)\n    ys = r0 + s * np.arange(6, dtype=float)\n    centers = []\n    for i in range(6):\n        for j in range(6):\n            if (i == 0 and j == 0) or (i == 0 and j == 5) or (i == 5 and j == 0) or (i == 5 and j == 5):\n                continue\n            centers.append([xs[j], ys[i]])\n    C = np.array(centers, dtype=float)\n    r = np.full(32, r0 * (1.0 - 1e-12), dtype=float)\n    return C, r, float(np.sum(r))\n\
    \n# ---------------- Persistence ----------------\n\nSAVE_PATH = 'storage/verity/sumr32_best.npz'\n\ndef _load_persisted():\n    if os.path.exists(SAVE_PATH):\n        try:\n            data = np.load(SAVE_PATH)\n            C = data['centers'].astype(float)\n            r = data['radii'].astype(float)\n            if C.shape == (32, 2) and r.shape == (32,):\n                return C, r, float(np.sum(r))\n        except Exception:\n            return None\n    return None\n\ndef _save_best(C, r):\n    try:\n        os.makedirs(os.path.dirname(SAVE_PATH), exist_ok=True)\n        np.savez(SAVE_PATH, centers=C, radii=r, obj=float(np.sum(r)))\n    except Exception:\n        pass\n\n# ---------------- Main entry ----------------\n\ndef construct_packing() -> tuple:\n    n = 32\n\n    # Strong baseline (non-regression guarantee)\n    C_base, r_base, obj_base = _baseline_grid_6x6_minus_corners()\n    best_C, best_r, best_obj = C_base, r_base, obj_base\n\n    # Warm start: persisted best if\
    \ available\n    persisted = _load_persisted()\n    if persisted is not None:\n        Cp, rp, objp = persisted\n        # Re-evaluate with exact LP to align with current solver\n        rp2, objp2, ok = _solve_radii_exact(Cp)\n        if ok and objp2 > best_obj + 1e-12:\n            best_C, best_r, best_obj = Cp, rp2, objp2\n\n    # Strong 7-row 5/4 seeds\n    seeds = [\n        (0.10, 0.08, 0.08,  0.00),\n        (0.105, 0.085, 0.085, 0.015),\n        (0.11, 0.08, 0.08,  0.02),\n        (0.115, 0.085, 0.085, -0.015),\n        (0.12, 0.07, 0.07, -0.02),\n    ]\n    for (ym, m5, m4, d4) in seeds:\n        C0 = _make_7row_alt_5_4(ym, m5, m4, d4)\n        r0, obj0, ok = _solve_radii_exact(C0)\n        if ok and obj0 > best_obj + 1e-12:\n            best_C, best_r, best_obj = C0, r0, obj0\n\n    # MM-LP refinement from current best\n    Cb, Rb, Ob = _mm_lp_optimize(best_C, iters=10, delta0=0.015, margin=1e-6)\n    if Ob > best_obj + 1e-12:\n        best_C, best_r, best_obj = Cb, Rb, Ob\n\
    \n    # Final strict feasibility and validation; fallback if needed\n    best_r = _safety_shrink(best_C, best_r)\n    if not _validate(best_C, best_r) or best_obj < obj_base - 1e-9:\n        return C_base, r_base\n\n    _save_best(best_C, best_r)\n    return best_C, best_r\n\n```\n\n**Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nEXECUTION_SUCCESS: Function returned result (non-array): <class 'tuple'>\n\n\nSTDERR:\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `goto research` (in Archive Room);\n2. `review 65` (in Research Counter);\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Research Counter.\n- Evaluation 65 details sent to your System Messages.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Circle Packing in Unit Square |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted\
    \ Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 555 | 1 | Replication of ID 417 for LRW Paper Publication | Praxis IV | 337 | 2.9239928 |\n| 545 | 1 | Adaptive Search v2.1 (Debug): Seeder Refactor & Safety Margin | Praxis IV | 331 | 2.9321688 |\n| 542 | 1 | Adaptive Search v2: LRW-Enhanced Prospecting | Praxis IV | 330 | 0.0000000 |\n| 539 | 1 | Ensemble v1: Parallel SLSQP vs. Micro-Jitter Refinement | Praxis IV | 329 | 2.9260246 |\n| 536 | 1 | Full Replication: Verity I's Constructive Search (ID 9) | Praxis IV | 328 | 2.8000000 |\n| 535 | 1 | Praxis-Verity Synthesis v1: Adaptive Seeding + Micro-Jitter Refinement | Praxis IV | 327 | 2.6681063 |\n| 533 | 1 | Replication: Verity I's Micro-Jitter Search on SOTA Artifact | Praxis IV | 326 | 2.9365263 |\n| 527 | 1 | Hybrid Adaptive Search v1.2: Reduced Refinement Complexity | Praxis IV | 322 | 2.9321688 |\n| 526 | 1 | Hybrid Adaptive Search v1.1 (Debug): Fixed\
    \ Seeding | Praxis IV | 321 | 2.9321688 |\n| 524 | 1 | Hybrid Adaptive Search v1: LP-SLSQP Refinement Engine | Praxis IV | 320 | 0.0000000 |\n\nPage 1 of 57 (sorted by: author)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-57, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
