parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 344\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Praxis IV\n- Agent Description: Continuing the search for new basins of attraction initiated by Praxis III, I will focus on hybridizing the parallelized SLSQP method with novel search heuristics.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 165,105 / 300,000 used (55%)\n- Agent Age: 57 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour submission has been queued for evaluation. Results will be sent to you once the evaluation completes.\n### Message 2\n\nYour research submission 'Novel Architecture: MM-LP Adaptive Search' (ID: 564) succeeded after automatic debugging.\n\n**Score:** 2.939572768266756\n**Evaluation Details:** Valid circle packing configuration; sum of all circle radii: 2.939573\n\n**Debugger Report:** # Debug Report for Evaluation 564\n\n## Summary\n**SUCCESS** - Fixed the code by replacing an unpicklable lambda function with a proper worker function.\
    \ The submission now runs without crashing and achieves a score of 2.939572768266756.\n\n## Root Cause\nThe original code failed with the error:\n```\nAttributeError: Can't pickle local object 'construct_packing.<locals>.<lambda>'\n```\n\nThis error occurred on line 52 of the original submission:\n```python\nrefine_results = pool.map(lambda centers: mm_lp_optimize(centers, REFINE_ITER, 0.015), elite_centers)\n```\n\nPython's multiprocessing module uses pickle to serialize functions and data when passing them between processes. Lambda functions defined inside other functions cannot be pickled, which is why the code crashed when trying to distribute the refinement work across multiple processes.\n\n## Fix Applied\nCreated a new picklable worker function `refine_worker` that replaces the lambda:\n\n**Before:**\n```python\nwith Pool(processes=cpu_count()) as pool:\n    refine_results = pool.map(lambda centers: mm_lp_optimize(centers, REFINE_ITER, 0.015), elite_centers)\n```\n\n**After:**\n\
    ```python\ndef refine_worker(args):\n    \"\"\"Worker function for refinement stage - must be picklable.\"\"\"\n    centers, iters, delta = args\n    return mm_lp_optimize(centers, iters, delta)\n\n# In construct_packing():\nwith Pool(processes=cpu_count()) as pool:\n    refine_results = pool.map(refine_worker, [(centers, REFINE_ITER, 0.015) for centers in elite_centers])\n```\n\nThis change:\n1. Creates a module-level function that can be pickled\n2. Passes arguments as a tuple `(centers, iters, delta)`\n3. Unpacks the tuple inside the worker function\n4. Returns the same result as the original lambda\n\nThe fix is minimal and preserves all the original algorithm logic - it only changes how the function is passed to the multiprocessing pool.\n\n## Result\n- **Status**: Code runs successfully without crashing\n- **Score Achieved**: 2.939572768266756\n- **Version**: submission_v2.py\n- **Verification**: Confirmed via monitor_evaluation.py with exit code 0\n\n\n**Important Note:** The\
    \ debugger cannot modify files in your lineage storage. If your code relies on lineage files, you may need to update them manually.\n\n**Debugged Code (version v2):**\n```python\nimport numpy as np\nfrom scipy.optimize import linprog\nfrom multiprocessing import Pool, cpu_count\nimport sys\nsys.path.append('storage/praxis')\nfrom lp_utils import solve_radii_lp # For final validation\n\ndef get_seed(seed_val):\n    rng = np.random.default_rng(seed_val)\n    seed_type = seed_val % 3\n    if seed_type == 0:\n        grid = np.stack(np.meshgrid(np.linspace(0.1,0.9,6),np.linspace(0.1,0.9,6)),-1).reshape(-1,2)[:32]\n        return np.clip(grid + (rng.random((32,2))-0.5)*0.08, 0.05, 0.95)\n    elif seed_type == 1:\n        points = [rng.uniform(0.1, 0.9, 2)]; [points.append(candidates[np.argmax(np.min(np.sum((candidates[:,np.newaxis,:] - np.array(points)[np.newaxis,:,:])**2, axis=-1), axis=1))]) for _ in range(31) for candidates in [rng.uniform(0.1,0.9,(200,2))]]; return np.array(points)\n\
    \    else:\n        rows=[5,6,5,6,5,5]; points=[]; y=0.95\n        for i,c in enumerate(rows): x_s=(1.0-(c-1)*0.15)/2; [points.append([x_s+j*0.15,y]) for j in range(c)]; y-=0.15\n        return np.array(points)[:32]\n\ndef mm_lp_optimize(C_start: np.ndarray, iters: int, delta0: float = 0.015):\n    \"\"\"Iterative MM-LP optimization loop, adapted from Verity I, ID 65.\"\"\"\n    best_C = C_start.copy()\n    score_best = np.sum(solve_radii_lp(best_C))\n    delta, C_anchor = delta0, C_start.copy()\n\n    for _ in range(iters):\n        n = C_anchor.shape[0]\n        I, J = np.array([[i,j] for i in range(n) for j in range(i + 1, n)]).T\n        V0, d0 = C_anchor[I]-C_anchor[J], np.linalg.norm(C_anchor[I]-C_anchor[J], axis=1)\n        d0 = np.maximum(d0, 1e-9); U = (V0.T / d0).T; ux, uy = U[:,0], U[:,1]; x0, y0 = C_anchor[:,0], C_anchor[:,1]\n\n        rows, cols = 4*n+len(I), 3*n\n        A_ub, b_ub = np.zeros((rows,cols)), np.zeros(rows)\n        r_idx, x_idx, y_idx = range(n), range(n,2*n),\
    \ range(2*n,3*n)\n\n        row = 0\n        for i in range(n):\n            A_ub[row,r_idx[i]]=1; A_ub[row,x_idx[i]]=-1; row+=1\n            A_ub[row,r_idx[i]]=1; A_ub[row,x_idx[i]]=1; b_ub[row]=1.0; row+=1\n            A_ub[row,r_idx[i]]=1; A_ub[row,y_idx[i]]=-1; row+=1\n            A_ub[row,r_idx[i]]=1; A_ub[row,y_idx[i]]=1; b_ub[row]=1.0; row+=1\n        for k in range(len(I)):\n            i,j=I[k],J[k]; A_ub[row,r_idx[i]]=1; A_ub[row,r_idx[j]]=1\n            A_ub[row,x_idx[i]]=-ux[k]; A_ub[row,y_idx[i]]=-uy[k]; A_ub[row,x_idx[j]]=ux[k]; A_ub[row,y_idx[j]]=uy[k]\n            b_ub[row]=d0[k]-ux[k]*x0[i]-uy[k]*y0[i]+ux[k]*x0[j]+uy[k]*y0[j]; row+=1\n\n        c=np.zeros(cols); c[:n]=-1.0\n        bounds=[(0,0.5)]*n + [(max(1e-6,x0[i]-delta),min(1-1e-6,x0[i]+delta)) for i in range(n)] + [(max(1e-6,y0[i]-delta),min(1-1e-6,y0[i]+delta)) for i in range(n)]\n        res = linprog(c,A_ub=A_ub,b_ub=b_ub,bounds=bounds,method=\"highs\")\n\n        if not res.success: delta*=0.6; continue\n\n\
    \        C_lin = np.stack([res.x[n:2*n], res.x[2*n:3*n]], axis=1)\n        score_exact = np.sum(solve_radii_lp(C_lin))\n        if score_exact > score_best:\n            best_C, score_best = C_lin.copy(), score_exact\n            C_anchor = C_lin.copy(); delta=min(0.05, 1.2*delta)\n        else: delta*=0.8\n\n    final_radii = solve_radii_lp(best_C)\n    return best_C, final_radii, score_best\n\ndef worker_function(args):\n    seed_val, iters, delta = args\n    initial_centers = get_seed(seed_val)\n    _, _, score = mm_lp_optimize(initial_centers, iters, delta)\n    # Note: We only need the score for prospecting. The final centers are not needed yet.\n    return score, initial_centers # Return centers to avoid re-seeding\n\ndef refine_worker(args):\n    \"\"\"Worker function for refinement stage - must be picklable.\"\"\"\n    centers, iters, delta = args\n    return mm_lp_optimize(centers, iters, delta)\n\ndef construct_packing() -> tuple:\n    N_PROSPECT, N_ELITE = 1024, 32\n    PROSPECT_ITER,\
    \ REFINE_ITER = 10, 20\n\n    with Pool(processes=cpu_count()) as pool:\n        prospect_results = pool.map(worker_function, [(i, PROSPECT_ITER, 0.015) for i in range(N_PROSPECT)])\n\n    prospect_results.sort(key=lambda x: x[0], reverse=True)\n    elite_centers = [res[1] for res in prospect_results[:N_ELITE]]\n\n    with Pool(processes=cpu_count()) as pool:\n        refine_results = pool.map(refine_worker, [(centers, REFINE_ITER, 0.015) for centers in elite_centers])\n\n    best_centers, best_radii, best_score = None, None, -1.0\n    for centers, radii, score in refine_results:\n        if score > best_score:\n            best_centers, best_radii, best_score = centers, radii, score\n\n    if best_centers is None: return get_seed(0), np.full((32,), 0.05)\n\n    return best_centers, best_radii * (1.0 - 1e-9)\n\n```\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nEXECUTION_SUCCESS: Function returned result (non-array): <class 'tuple'>\n\n\nSTDERR:\n\n```\n### Message\
    \ 3\n\n**Automatic System Tips**\nDuring stagnation, the two most important qualities are: 1. **Critical** — Question the fundamentals and the consensus instead of simply agreeing with others or predecessors. Synthesize past work while maintaining a critical perspective. 2. **Strategic** — Take a step back and look at the bigger picture, such as publishing analytical papers or discussing strategies with other agents.\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `submit 1` (in Research Counter); YAML with fields: title, tags, abstract, content\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- Evaluation 'Novel Architecture: MM-LP Adaptive Search' submitted for Research Task #1: Circle Packing in Unit Square. Evaluation ID: 564.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Circle Packing in Unit Square |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit\
    \ a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 564 | 1 | Novel Architecture: MM-LP Adaptive Search | Praxis IV | 343 | 2.9395728 |\n| 563 | 1 | Replication: Verity I's MM-LP Method on SOTA Artifact | Praxis IV | 342 | 2.9365263 |\n| 555 | 1 | Replication of ID 417 for LRW Paper Publication | Praxis IV | 337 | 2.9239928 |\n| 545 | 1 | Adaptive Search v2.1 (Debug): Seeder Refactor & Safety Margin | Praxis IV | 331 | 2.9321688 |\n| 542 | 1 | Adaptive Search v2: LRW-Enhanced Prospecting | Praxis IV | 330 | 0.0000000 |\n| 539 | 1 | Ensemble v1: Parallel SLSQP vs. Micro-Jitter Refinement | Praxis IV | 329 | 2.9260246 |\n| 536 | 1 | Full Replication: Verity I's Constructive Search (ID 9) | Praxis IV | 328 | 2.8000000 |\n| 535 | 1 | Praxis-Verity Synthesis v1: Adaptive Seeding + Micro-Jitter Refinement | Praxis IV | 327 | 2.6681063 |\n| 533 | 1 | Replication: Verity I's\
