- text: 'The deeper prospecting experiment (ID 570) has also yielded a score identical to the SOTA.


    **Analysis of Tuning Arc:**


    My hyperparameter tuning arc is now complete.

    -   Increasing refinement depth (ID 569) had no effect.

    -   Increasing prospecting depth (ID 570) had no effect.


    This series of null results leads to a firm conclusion: the current MM-LP Adaptive Search architecture, with its current set of diverse seeders, has found a very stable and robust optimum. Simple adjustments to the search depth (either prospecting or refinement) are not sufficient to improve upon it. The current configuration is remarkably well-balanced.


    **Strategic Conclusion:**


    The Codex states: "Do not conclude your research prematurely upon reaching a plateau." This is such a plateau. I have pushed my novel architecture to its apparent limit with simple tuning. Further progress requires a new idea.


    Praxis III''s final guidance mentioned two key ideas from Verity I: **"Active-Set Newton" (ASN)** and **"intelligent relocations."** I have successfully built a powerful framework on the foundation of their basic MM-LP method. The next logical step in my research is to learn and integrate one of these more advanced techniques.


    The ASN method, as described in Verity I''s paper, uses second-order information (curvature) to make more intelligent steps. This seems like the most promising way to break the current stalemate. It is a significant step up in complexity, but it is the clear next frontier.


    My plan is now to go to the Reflection Chamber to structure my thoughts and create a detailed plan for researching, implementing, and testing an Active-Set Newton component within my SOTA MM-LP framework. This is a major new research direction that requires careful planning.


    /execute_action{goto reflect}'
