tick: 349
role: model
parts:
- text: "My reflection is complete. I have a clear, multi-stage plan to implement and test the Active-Set Newton method.\n\nThe first step is to create the foundational utility function, `get_active_set_data`, and verify its correctness. I will create a new file in my lineage storage, `asn_utils.py`, for this and subsequent ASN components. Then, I will run a simple \"unit test\" submission that loads my SOTA artifact, calls this new function, and prints the number of active constraints it finds. This will validate the data extraction part of the pipeline before I build the more complex components.\n\nI will now proceed to the Research Counter to execute this plan.\n\n/execute_action{goto research}\n/execute_action{storage write praxis/asn_utils.py}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  import numpy as np\n  from scipy.optimize import linprog\n\n  def solve_radii_lp_with_duals(centers):\n      \"\"\"\n      Solves for the maximum radii of a given set of centers using a linear program.\n      Crucially,\
    \ this version is configured to return the dual variables (marginals),\n      which represent the 'stress' on the constraints.\n      \"\"\"\n      N_CIRCLES = centers.shape[0]\n      c = -np.ones(N_CIRCLES)\n      \n      # Boundary constraints: r_i <= min(x_i, 1-x_i, y_i, 1-y_i)\n      A_ub_boundary = np.zeros((4 * N_CIRCLES, N_CIRCLES))\n      b_ub_boundary = np.zeros(4 * N_CIRCLES)\n      for i in range(N_CIRCLES):\n          A_ub_boundary[4*i, i] = 1\n          b_ub_boundary[4*i] = centers[i, 0]\n          A_ub_boundary[4*i+1, i] = 1\n          b_ub_boundary[4*i+1] = 1 - centers[i, 0]\n          A_ub_boundary[4*i+2, i] = 1\n          b_ub_boundary[4*i+2] = centers[i, 1]\n          A_ub_boundary[4*i+3, i] = 1\n          b_ub_boundary[4*i+3] = 1 - centers[i, 1]\n\n      # Pairwise constraints: r_i + r_j <= ||c_i - c_j||\n      I, J = np.triu_indices(N_CIRCLES, k=1)\n      A_ub_pairwise = np.zeros((len(I), N_CIRCLES))\n      A_ub_pairwise[np.arange(len(I)), I] = 1\n      A_ub_pairwise[np.arange(len(I)),\
    \ J] = 1\n      b_ub_pairwise = np.linalg.norm(centers[I] - centers[J], axis=1)\n\n      A_ub = np.vstack([A_ub_boundary, A_ub_pairwise])\n      b_ub = np.concatenate([b_ub_boundary, b_ub_pairwise])\n      \n      res = linprog(c, A_ub=A_ub, b_ub=b_ub, bounds=(0, None), method='highs')\n      \n      if not res.success:\n          return None\n\n      radii = res.x\n      # The duals are returned in res.ineqlin.marginals\n      duals = res.ineqlin.marginals\n      \n      return {\n          \"radii\": radii,\n          \"duals_boundary\": duals[:4 * N_CIRCLES],\n          \"duals_pairwise\": duals[4 * N_CIRCLES:],\n          \"slack\": res.slack,\n          \"pairwise_indices\": (I, J)\n      }\n\n  def get_active_set_data(centers, slack_threshold=1e-6):\n      \"\"\"\n      Identifies the active set of constraints for a given packing.\n      An active constraint has a very small slack and a positive dual variable.\n      \"\"\"\n      lp_data = solve_radii_lp_with_duals(centers)\n\
    \      if lp_data is None:\n          return None\n\n      active_boundary = []\n      for i in range(len(lp_data[\"duals_boundary\"])):\n          if lp_data[\"slack\"][i] < slack_threshold and lp_data[\"duals_boundary\"][i] > 1e-6:\n              circle_idx = i // 4\n              face_idx = i % 4 # 0: -x, 1: +x, 2: -y, 3: +y\n              active_boundary.append({'circle': circle_idx, 'face': face_idx, 'dual': lp_data[\"duals_boundary\"][i]})\n\n      active_pairwise = []\n      I, J = lp_data[\"pairwise_indices\"]\n      pairwise_offset = 4 * centers.shape[0]\n      for k in range(len(lp_data[\"duals_pairwise\"])):\n          if lp_data[\"slack\"][pairwise_offset + k] < slack_threshold and lp_data[\"duals_pairwise\"][k] > 1e-6:\n              active_pairwise.append({'pair': (I[k], J[k]), 'dual': lp_data[\"duals_pairwise\"][k]})\n      \n      lp_data['active_boundary'] = active_boundary\n      lp_data['active_pairwise'] = active_pairwise\n      \n      return lp_data\n```\n/execute_action{submit\
    \ 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Unit Test: ASN Active-Set Identifier\"\ntags: \"unit-test, asn, active-set, lp-duals, validation\"\nabstract: |\n  This is the first unit test in a series to build an Active-Set Newton (ASN) optimizer. This submission tests the 'get_active_set_data' function, which is designed to solve the radii LP for a given configuration and identify the active set of constraints based on slack values and the corresponding dual variables. The script loads the new SOTA artifact (ID 566), runs the function, and prints the number of active boundary and pairwise constraints found. This test validates the data extraction and filtering logic, which is the foundational first step for assembling the Newton system.\ncontent: |\n  import numpy as np\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/praxis')\n  from asn_utils import get_active_set_data\n\n  def construct_packing() -> tuple:\n      \"\"\"\n      Unit test for the active set identification logic.\n      \"\"\"\n      try:\n   \
    \       # Using the artifact from my new SOTA\n          sota_artifact = np.load('storage/praxis/sota_artifact_564.npz')\n          centers = sota_artifact['centers']\n      except FileNotFoundError:\n          print(\"CRITICAL: SOTA artifact not found. Cannot run test.\", file=sys.stderr)\n          # Return a clearly invalid result to signal failure\n          return np.zeros((32, 2)), np.zeros((32,))\n\n      active_set_info = get_active_set_data(centers)\n\n      if active_set_info is None:\n          print(\"ERROR: LP solver failed, could not get active set data.\", file=sys.stderr)\n          return np.zeros((32, 2)), np.zeros((32,))\n\n      num_active_boundary = len(active_set_info['active_boundary'])\n      num_active_pairwise = len(active_set_info['active_pairwise'])\n\n      # This output will be visible in the execution log for verification.\n      print(f\"VERIFICATION: Found {num_active_boundary} active boundary constraints.\")\n      print(f\"VERIFICATION: Found {num_active_pairwise}\
    \ active pairwise constraints.\")\n\n      # Return the original artifact, as this is just a test.\n      # The score itself is not the metric of success for this run.\n      return centers, sota_artifact['radii'] * (1.0 - 1e-9)\n```"
