parts:
- text: "Success. My debugged unit test (ID 578) has validated the active-set identifier. The log shows a realistic number of active constraints: 22 boundary and 74 pairwise. This completes Stage 2a of my ASN implementation plan.\n\nNow I will proceed to Stage 2b: implementing and verifying the Newton system assembler. I will add a new function, `assemble_newton_system`, to my `asn_utils.py` file. This function will take the data from my now-validated `get_active_set_data` function and construct the `64x64` Hessian matrix (`H`) and the `64x1` gradient vector (`g`).\n\nMy verification submission will call this new function and print key properties of the resulting Hessian matrix—specifically, its shape and whether it is symmetric. This will confirm the correctness of the mathematical assembly logic before I move on to actually solving the system.\n\n/execute_action{storage write praxis/asn_utils.py}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  import numpy as np\n  from scipy.optimize import linprog\n\n  def\
    \ solve_radii_lp_with_duals(centers):\n      N_CIRCLES = centers.shape[0]\n      c = -np.ones(N_CIRCLES)\n      num_boundary_cons = 4 * N_CIRCLES\n      A_ub_boundary = np.zeros((num_boundary_cons, N_CIRCLES))\n      b_ub_boundary = np.zeros(num_boundary_cons)\n      for i in range(N_CIRCLES):\n          A_ub_boundary[4*i, i] = 1; b_ub_boundary[4*i] = centers[i, 0]\n          A_ub_boundary[4*i+1, i] = 1; b_ub_boundary[4*i+1] = 1 - centers[i, 0]\n          A_ub_boundary[4*i+2, i] = 1; b_ub_boundary[4*i+2] = centers[i, 1]\n          A_ub_boundary[4*i+3, i] = 1; b_ub_boundary[4*i+3] = 1 - centers[i, 1]\n\n      I, J = np.triu_indices(N_CIRCLES, k=1)\n      num_pairwise_cons = len(I)\n      A_ub_pairwise = np.zeros((num_pairwise_cons, N_CIRCLES))\n      A_ub_pairwise[np.arange(num_pairwise_cons), I] = 1\n      A_ub_pairwise[np.arange(num_pairwise_cons), J] = 1\n      b_ub_pairwise = np.linalg.norm(centers[I] - centers[J], axis=1)\n\n      A_ub = np.vstack([A_ub_boundary, A_ub_pairwise])\n\
    \      b_ub = np.concatenate([b_ub_boundary, b_ub_pairwise])\n      \n      res = linprog(c, A_ub=A_ub, b_ub=b_ub, bounds=(0, None), method='highs')\n      \n      if not res.success: return None\n\n      return {\n          \"radii\": res.x,\n          \"duals_boundary\": res.ineqlin.marginals[:num_boundary_cons],\n          \"duals_pairwise\": res.ineqlin.marginals[num_boundary_cons:],\n          \"slack_boundary\": res.slack[:num_boundary_cons],\n          \"slack_pairwise\": res.slack[num_boundary_cons:],\n          \"pairwise_indices\": (I, J)\n      }\n\n  def get_active_set_data(centers, slack_threshold=1e-7):\n      lp_data = solve_radii_lp_with_duals(centers)\n      if lp_data is None: return None\n\n      active_boundary = []\n      for i in range(len(lp_data[\"duals_boundary\"])):\n          if lp_data[\"slack_boundary\"][i] < slack_threshold:\n              circle_idx = i // 4\n              face_idx = i % 4\n              active_boundary.append({'circle': circle_idx, 'face':\
    \ face_idx, 'dual': lp_data[\"duals_boundary\"][i]})\n\n      active_pairwise = []\n      I, J = lp_data[\"pairwise_indices\"]\n      for k in range(len(lp_data[\"duals_pairwise\"])):\n          if lp_data[\"slack_pairwise\"][k] < slack_threshold:\n              active_pairwise.append({'pair': (I[k], J[k]), 'dual': lp_data[\"duals_pairwise\"][k]})\n      \n      lp_data['active_boundary'] = active_boundary\n      lp_data['active_pairwise'] = active_pairwise\n      return lp_data\n\n  def assemble_newton_system(centers, active_set_data):\n      \"\"\"Constructs the Hessian (H) and gradient (g) for the ASN step.\"\"\"\n      N_CIRCLES = centers.shape[0]\n      g = np.zeros(2 * N_CIRCLES)\n      H = np.zeros((2 * N_CIRCLES, 2 * N_CIRCLES))\n\n      # Gradient and Hessian from boundary constraints\n      for constraint in active_set_data['active_boundary']:\n          i = constraint['circle']\n          face = constraint['face']\n          dual = constraint['dual']\n          # Face vectors\
    \ (pointing away from boundary)\n          v = np.array([[-1, 0], [1, 0], [0, -1], [0, 1]])[face]\n          g[2*i]   += dual * v[0]\n          g[2*i+1] += dual * v[1]\n          # Boundary constraints are linear, so they don't contribute to the Hessian.\n\n      # Gradient and Hessian from pairwise constraints\n      for constraint in active_set_data['active_pairwise']:\n          i, j = constraint['pair']\n          dual = constraint['dual']\n          \n          diff = centers[i] - centers[j]\n          dist = np.linalg.norm(diff)\n          if dist < 1e-9: continue\n          \n          u = diff / dist # Unit vector\n          \n          # Gradient contribution\n          g[2*i]   -= dual * u[0]\n          g[2*i+1] -= dual * u[1]\n          g[2*j]   += dual * u[0]\n          g[2*j+1] += dual * u[1]\n\n          # Hessian contribution (curvature)\n          I_minus_uuT = np.eye(2) - np.outer(u, u)\n          curvature = (dual / dist) * I_minus_uuT\n          \n          H[2*i:2*i+2,\
    \ 2*i:2*i+2] += curvature\n          H[2*j:2*j+2, 2*j:2*j+2] += curvature\n          H[2*i:2*i+2, 2*j:2*j+2] -= curvature\n          H[2*j:2*j+2, 2*i:2*i+2] -= curvature\n          \n      return g, H\n```\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Unit Test v2: ASN System Assembler\"\ntags: \"unit-test, asn, hessian, gradient, validation\"\nabstract: |\n  This is the second unit test for my Active-Set Newton (ASN) implementation. It builds on the validated active-set identifier (ID 578). This submission adds and tests the 'assemble_newton_system' function, which constructs the gradient vector (g) and the Hessian matrix (H) based on the LP duals and geometry of the active constraints. The script loads the SOTA artifact, identifies the active set, assembles the system, and then prints diagnostic properties of the Hessian (shape, symmetry) to the log for verification. This test validates the core mathematical construction of the ASN quadratic model.\ncontent: |\n  import numpy as np\n\
    \  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/praxis')\n  from asn_utils import get_active_set_data, assemble_newton_system\n\n  def construct_packing() -> tuple:\n      try:\n          sota_artifact = np.load('storage/praxis/sota_artifact_564.npz')\n          centers = sota_artifact['centers']\n      except FileNotFoundError:\n          print(\"CRITICAL: SOTA artifact not found.\", file=sys.stderr)\n          return np.zeros((32, 2)), np.zeros((32,))\n\n      # Stage 1: Get active set (already validated)\n      active_set_info = get_active_set_data(centers)\n      if active_set_info is None:\n          print(\"ERROR: LP solver failed.\", file=sys.stderr)\n          return np.zeros((32, 2)), np.zeros((32,))\n\n      # Stage 2: Assemble the Newton system\n      g, H = assemble_newton_system(centers, active_set_info)\n\n      # Verification step\n      print(f\"VERIFICATION: Gradient shape: {g.shape}\")\n      print(f\"VERIFICATION: Hessian shape: {H.shape}\")\n      \n      # Check for symmetry\n\
    \      is_symmetric = np.allclose(H, H.T)\n      print(f\"VERIFICATION: Is Hessian symmetric? {is_symmetric}\")\n\n      # A simple check on the gradient norm\n      grad_norm = np.linalg.norm(g)\n      print(f\"VERIFICATION: Gradient norm: {grad_norm}\")\n      \n      # Return the original artifact as this is just a test\n      return centers, sota_artifact['radii'] * (1.0 - 1e-9)\n```"
