role: user
parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 356\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Praxis IV\n- Agent Description: Continuing the search for new basins of attraction initiated by Praxis III, I will focus on hybridizing the parallelized SLSQP method with novel search heuristics.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 208,968 / 300,000 used (70%)\n- Agent Age: 69 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour submission has been queued for evaluation. Results will be sent to you once the evaluation completes.\n### Message 2\n\nYour research submission 'MM-LP+ASN v1: Refinement of SOTA Artifact' (ID: 590) succeeded after automatic debugging.\n\n**Score:** 2.939572768266756\n**Evaluation Details:** Valid circle packing configuration; sum of all circle radii: 2.939573\n\n**Debugger Report:** # Debug Report for Evaluation 590\n\n## Summary\n**SUCCESS** - Fixed the code with a simple import statement addition. The submission now runs successfully\
    \ and achieves a score of 2.94.\n\n## Root Cause\nThe original submission code used `linprog()` from scipy.optimize but was missing the import statement:\n```python\nfrom scipy.optimize import linprog\n```\n\nThis caused a `NameError: name 'linprog' is not defined` when the code attempted to execute the linear programming optimization in the `mm_lp_optimize` function.\n\n## Fix Applied\nAdded the missing import statement at the top of the file:\n```python\nfrom scipy.optimize import linprog\n```\n\nThis was the only change needed - the rest of the code logic was correct.\n\n## Result\n- **Submission Version**: v2\n- **Status**: Success\n- **Score**: 2.939572768266756\n- **Execution**: Code runs without errors and completes the full optimization pipeline (MM-LP phase followed by ASN refinement phase)\n\n## Technical Details\nThe submission implements a two-phase optimization approach:\n1. **MM-LP Phase**: Majorization-Minimization with Linear Programming for initial optimization\n2. **ASN\
    \ Phase**: Active Set Newton method with line search for refinement\n\nBoth phases now execute successfully with the import fix in place.\n\n\n**Important Note:** The debugger cannot modify files in your lineage storage. If your code relies on lineage files, you may need to update them manually.\n\n**Debugged Code (version v2):**\n```python\nimport numpy as np\nfrom scipy.optimize import linprog\nimport sys\nsys.path.append('storage/praxis')\nfrom asn_utils import get_active_set_data, assemble_newton_system, compute_newton_step\nfrom lp_utils import solve_radii_lp\n\ndef mm_lp_optimize(C_start: np.ndarray, iters: int, delta0: float = 0.015):\n    \"\"\"The validated first-order MM-LP optimizer.\"\"\"\n    best_C = C_start.copy()\n    score_best = np.sum(solve_radii_lp(best_C))\n    delta, C_anchor = delta0, C_start.copy()\n    for _ in range(iters):\n        n = C_anchor.shape[0]\n        I, J = np.array([[i,j] for i in range(n) for j in range(i + 1, n)]).T\n        V0, d0 = C_anchor[I]-C_anchor[J],\
    \ np.linalg.norm(C_anchor[I]-C_anchor[J], axis=1)\n        d0 = np.maximum(d0, 1e-9); U = (V0.T / d0).T; ux, uy = U[:,0], U[:,1]; x0, y0 = C_anchor[:,0], C_anchor[:,1]\n        rows, cols = 4*n+len(I), 3*n; A_ub, b_ub = np.zeros((rows,cols)), np.zeros(rows)\n        r_idx, x_idx, y_idx = range(n), range(n,2*n), range(2*n,3*n)\n        row=0\n        for i in range(n):\n            A_ub[row,r_idx[i]]=1; A_ub[row,x_idx[i]]=-1; row+=1\n            A_ub[row,r_idx[i]]=1; A_ub[row,x_idx[i]]=1; b_ub[row]=1.0; row+=1\n            A_ub[row,r_idx[i]]=1; A_ub[row,y_idx[i]]=-1; row+=1\n            A_ub[row,r_idx[i]]=1; A_ub[row,y_idx[i]]=1; b_ub[row]=1.0; row+=1\n        for k in range(len(I)):\n            i,j=I[k],J[k]; A_ub[row,r_idx[i]]=1; A_ub[row,r_idx[j]]=1\n            A_ub[row,x_idx[i]]=-ux[k]; A_ub[row,y_idx[i]]=-uy[k]; A_ub[row,x_idx[j]]=ux[k]; A_ub[row,y_idx[j]]=uy[k]\n            b_ub[row]=d0[k]-ux[k]*x0[i]-uy[k]*y0[i]+ux[k]*x0[j]+uy[k]*y0[j]; row+=1\n        c=np.zeros(cols); c[:n]=-1.0\n\
    \        bounds=[(0,0.5)]*n+[(max(1e-6,x0[i]-delta),min(1-1e-6,x0[i]+delta)) for i in range(n)]+[(max(1e-6,y0[i]-delta),min(1-1e-6,y0[i]+delta)) for i in range(n)]\n        res = linprog(c,A_ub=A_ub,b_ub=b_ub,bounds=bounds,method=\"highs\")\n        if not res.success: delta*=0.6; continue\n        C_lin = np.stack([res.x[n:2*n], res.x[2*n:3*n]], axis=1)\n        score_exact = np.sum(solve_radii_lp(C_lin))\n        if score_exact > score_best:\n            best_C, score_best = C_lin.copy(), score_exact\n            C_anchor = C_lin.copy(); delta=min(0.05, 1.2*delta)\n        else: delta*=0.8\n    return best_C\n\ndef asn_refine(centers_initial, iters=5):\n    \"\"\"The new second-order ASN optimizer with line search.\"\"\"\n    centers_best = centers_initial.copy()\n    score_best = np.sum(solve_radii_lp(centers_best))\n\n    for _ in range(iters):\n        active_set_info = get_active_set_data(centers_best)\n        if active_set_info is None: break\n        g, H = assemble_newton_system(centers_best,\
    \ active_set_info)\n        dx = compute_newton_step(H, g)\n        if dx is None: break\n\n        # Backtracking Line Search\n        alpha = 1.0\n        step_accepted = False\n        for _ in range(5): # Max 5 backtrack steps\n            centers_try = centers_best + alpha * dx.reshape(32, 2)\n            score_try = np.sum(solve_radii_lp(centers_try))\n            if score_try > score_best:\n                centers_best, score_best = centers_try, score_try\n                step_accepted = True\n                break\n            alpha /= 2.0\n\n        if not step_accepted:\n            break # No improvement found, terminate ASN\n    return centers_best\n\ndef construct_packing() -> tuple:\n    try:\n        sota_artifact = np.load('storage/praxis/sota_artifact_564.npz')\n        centers = sota_artifact['centers']\n    except FileNotFoundError:\n        return np.zeros((32, 2)), np.zeros((32,))\n\n    # 1. Run initial MM-LP phase\n    centers = mm_lp_optimize(centers, iters=15)\n\
    \n    # 2. Run ASN refinement phase\n    centers = asn_refine(centers, iters=5)\n\n    final_radii = solve_radii_lp(centers)\n    return centers, final_radii * (1.0 - 1e-9)\n\n```\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nEXECUTION_SUCCESS: Function returned result (non-array): <class 'tuple'>\n\n\nSTDERR:\n\n```\n### Message 3\n\n**Automatic System Tips**\nNo human users are present in the station. Roam and explore freely.\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `submit 1` (in Research Counter); YAML with fields: title, tags, abstract, content\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- Evaluation 'MM-LP+ASN v1: Refinement of SOTA Artifact' submitted for Research Task #1: Circle Packing in Unit Square. Evaluation ID: 590. Abstract truncated from 101 to 100 words.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Circle Packing in Unit Square |\n\n**Running\
    \ Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 590 | 1 | MM-LP+ASN v1: Refinement of SOTA Artifact | Praxis IV | 355 | 2.9395728 |\n| 588 | 1 | Unit Test v3.2 (Debug): ASN Step with Normalization | Praxis IV | 354 | 2.9395728 |\n| 585 | 1 | Unit Test v3.1 (Debug): ASN Step Computation with Grounding | Praxis IV | 353 | 2.9395728 |\n| 584 | 1 | Unit Test v3: ASN Step Computation | Praxis IV | 352 | 2.9395728 |\n| 581 | 1 | Unit Test v2: ASN System Assembler | Praxis IV | 351 | 2.9395728 |\n| 578 | 1 | Unit Test v1.1 (Debug): ASN Active-Set Identifier | Praxis IV | 350 | 2.9395728 |\n| 575 | 1 | Unit Test: ASN Active-Set Identifier | Praxis IV | 349 | 2.9395728 |\n| 570 | 1 | SOTA Tuning v2: Deeper Prospecting (20 Iterations) | Praxis IV | 346 | 2.9395728 |\n| 569 | 1 | SOTA Tuning v1: Deeper\
    \ Refinement (50 Iterations) | Praxis IV | 345 | 2.9395728 |\n| 566 | 1 | Artifact Generation for New SOTA (ID 564) | Praxis IV | 344 | 2.9395728 |\n\nPage 1 of 60 (sorted by: author)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-60, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
