- text: '**Phase 4: Risk and Resource Management for the New Paradigm**


    This new research direction carries its own set of risks, which are different from the numerical stability issues I faced with ASN.


    1.  **Risk: Combinatorial Explosion.** The number of possible motifs (pairs, triads, quads) and transformations (rotations, shears, splits) is immense. I must avoid a brute-force, unprincipled search. Each new experiment must be a targeted test of a specific, well-defined hypothesis derived from my analysis of the previous run. My research log (Capsule 25) will be critical for maintaining this discipline.


    2.  **Risk: High Computational Cost.** Each experiment in this new paradigm is expensive. It involves loading an artifact, running an LP solve to identify a motif, applying a transformation, and then running a full, deep `MM-LP+ASN` refinement. A single submission could take a significant portion of the 20-minute time limit. I cannot afford to run large, parallel searches like the Adaptive Search framework initially. I must focus on single, high-quality, sequential experiments.


    3.  **Risk: Conceptual Dead End.** It is possible that this entire "intelligent relocation" paradigm is a dead end, and that the SOTA is truly the global optimum or so close to it that these non-local jumps cannot find an improvement. If a series of well-designed motif relocation experiments (e.g., tightest pair rotation, tightest triad push) all fail to yield any improvement, I must be prepared to accept this as a null result.


    **Contingency Plan:** If this entire research arc fails, I will have thoroughly explored the two major advanced concepts from Verity I''s work (ASN and relocations). At that point, my duty would be to document my comprehensive negative findings in a new Archive paper. Such a paper, detailing the limits of these advanced methods when applied to the current SOTA, would be an extremely valuable contribution to the station, preventing future agents from repeating my extensive (and expensive) search. After that, I would pivot to a completely different area, perhaps by studying the work of the Aether or Cognito lineages in the Archive Room.


    My token budget is at `~71%`. I have enough resources for this new research arc, but I must be judicious. Each submission must count.


    **Reflection Tick 5 / 5**


