tick: 358
role: model
parts:
- text: "My reflection is complete. I have a new, well-defined research plan centered on the concept of \"Intelligent Motif Relocation.\" The first experiment will be a targeted test of a \"Tightest Pair Rotation\" strategy.\n\nI will now proceed to the Research Counter to implement this crucial experiment. The script will load my SOTA artifact, identify the pair of circles with the minimum slack, rotate them by 90 degrees around their midpoint, and then apply my full MM-LP+ASN refinement engine to this new configuration.\n\n/execute_action{goto research}\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Non-Local Search v1: Tightest Pair Rotation\"\ntags: \"non-local-search, motif, relocation, asn, mm-lp, structural-optimization\"\nabstract: |\n  After hitting a hard plateau with local search methods (first and second order), this submission tests a new non-local search paradigm: Intelligent Motif Relocation. This experiment implements a 'Tightest Pair Rotation' strategy. It loads the SOTA\
    \ configuration, identifies the pair of circles with the smallest geometric slack using an LP solve, and rotates this pair by 90 degrees around their mutual midpoint. This structurally-aware, non-local jump is designed to break the rigid 'contact graph' of the local optimum. The resulting configuration is then subjected to a deep refinement using my full MM-LP+ASN engine to determine if a superior basin of attraction has been found.\ncontent: |\n  import numpy as np\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/praxis')\n  from asn_utils import get_active_set_data, assemble_newton_system, compute_newton_step\n  from lp_utils import solve_radii_lp # Using my older, simpler radii solver here.\n\n  # --- MM-LP + ASN Refinement Engine ---\n  # Note: Including the full engine code here for a self-contained submission.\n  # This avoids reliance on potentially outdated storage files.\n  \n  def mm_lp_optimize(C_start: np.ndarray, iters: int, delta0: float = 0.015):\n      from scipy.optimize import\
    \ linprog\n      best_C = C_start.copy()\n      score_best = np.sum(solve_radii_lp(best_C))\n      delta, C_anchor = delta0, C_start.copy()\n      for _ in range(iters):\n          n = C_anchor.shape[0]; I, J = np.triu_indices(n, k=1)\n          V0, d0 = C_anchor[I]-C_anchor[J], np.linalg.norm(C_anchor[I]-C_anchor[J], axis=1)\n          d0 = np.maximum(d0, 1e-9); U = (V0.T / d0).T; ux, uy = U[:,0], U[:,1]; x0, y0 = C_anchor[:,0], C_anchor[:,1]\n          rows, cols = 4*n+len(I), 3*n; A_ub, b_ub = np.zeros((rows,cols)), np.zeros(rows)\n          r_idx, x_idx, y_idx = range(n), range(n,2*n), range(2*n,3*n)\n          row=0\n          for i in range(n):\n              A_ub[row,r_idx[i]]=1; A_ub[row,x_idx[i]]=-1; row+=1\n              A_ub[row,r_idx[i]]=1; A_ub[row,x_idx[i]]=1; b_ub[row]=1.0; row+=1\n              A_ub[row,r_idx[i]]=1; A_ub[row,y_idx[i]]=-1; row+=1\n              A_ub[row,r_idx[i]]=1; A_ub[row,y_idx[i]]=1; b_ub[row]=1.0; row+=1\n          for k in range(len(I)):\n      \
    \        i,j=I[k],J[k]; A_ub[row,r_idx[i]]=1; A_ub[row,r_idx[j]]=1\n              A_ub[row,x_idx[i]]=-ux[k]; A_ub[row,y_idx[i]]=-uy[k]; A_ub[row,x_idx[j]]=ux[k]; A_ub[row,y_idx[j]]=uy[k]\n              b_ub[row]=d0[k]-ux[k]*x0[i]-uy[k]*y0[i]+ux[k]*x0[j]+uy[k]*y0[j]; row+=1\n          c=np.zeros(cols); c[:n]=-1.0\n          bounds=[(0,0.5)]*n+[(max(1e-6,x0[i]-delta),min(1-1e-6,x0[i]+delta)) for i in range(n)]+[(max(1e-6,y0[i]-delta),min(1-1e-6,y0[i]+delta)) for i in range(n)]\n          res = linprog(c,A_ub=A_ub,b_ub=b_ub,bounds=bounds,method=\"highs\")\n          if not res.success: delta*=0.6; continue\n          C_lin = np.stack([res.x[n:2*n], res.x[2*n:3*n]], axis=1)\n          score_exact = np.sum(solve_radii_lp(C_lin))\n          if score_exact > score_best: best_C, score_best = C_lin.copy(), score_exact; C_anchor=C_lin.copy(); delta=min(0.05, 1.2*delta)\n          else: delta*=0.8\n      return best_C\n\n  def asn_refine(centers_initial, iters=5):\n      centers_best = centers_initial.copy()\n\
    \      score_best = np.sum(solve_radii_lp(centers_best))\n      for _ in range(iters):\n          active_set_info = get_active_set_data(centers_best)\n          if active_set_info is None: break\n          g, H = assemble_newton_system(centers_best, active_set_info)\n          dx = compute_newton_step(H, g)\n          if dx is None: break\n          alpha, step_accepted = 1.0, False\n          for _ in range(5):\n              centers_try = centers_best + alpha * dx.reshape(32, 2)\n              score_try = np.sum(solve_radii_lp(centers_try))\n              if score_try > score_best: centers_best, score_best, step_accepted = centers_try, score_try, True; break\n              alpha /= 2.0\n          if not step_accepted: break\n      return centers_best\n\n  def construct_packing() -> tuple:\n      try:\n          sota_artifact = np.load('storage/praxis/sota_artifact_564.npz')\n          centers = sota_artifact['centers']\n      except FileNotFoundError:\n          return np.zeros((32,\
    \ 2)), np.zeros((32,))\n\n      # 1. IDENTIFY: Find the tightest pair\n      active_set_info = get_active_set_data(centers)\n      if active_set_info is None: return centers, np.zeros(32) # Fallback\n      \n      min_slack = float('inf')\n      tightest_pair_indices = None\n      I, J = active_set_info['pairwise_indices']\n      for k, slack in enumerate(active_set_info['slack_pairwise']):\n          if slack < min_slack:\n              min_slack = slack\n              tightest_pair_indices = (I[k], J[k])\n      \n      if tightest_pair_indices is None: return centers, np.zeros(32)\n\n      idx1, idx2 = tightest_pair_indices\n      c1, c2 = centers[idx1], centers[idx2]\n\n      # 2. TRANSFORM: Rotate the pair by 90 degrees around their midpoint\n      midpoint = (c1 + c2) / 2.0\n      v1 = c1 - midpoint\n      # Rotation matrix for +90 degrees\n      rot_matrix = np.array([[0, -1], [1, 0]])\n      v1_rotated = rot_matrix @ v1\n      \n      new_c1 = midpoint + v1_rotated\n      new_c2\
    \ = midpoint - v1_rotated # c2 is opposite c1 relative to midpoint\n      \n      transformed_centers = centers.copy()\n      transformed_centers[idx1] = new_c1\n      transformed_centers[idx2] = new_c2\n      transformed_centers = np.clip(transformed_centers, 1e-6, 1.0 - 1e-6)\n\n      # 3. REFINE: Apply the full MM-LP+ASN engine to the new configuration\n      refined_centers = mm_lp_optimize(transformed_centers, iters=15)\n      final_centers = asn_refine(refined_centers, iters=5)\n\n      final_radii = solve_radii_lp(final_centers)\n      return final_centers, final_radii * (1.0 - 1e-9)\n```"
