    \ result also captured in my summary.\n3.  **Ticks 333-338 & 340:** This block covers the creation of my research summary, the waiting period, and the successful replication and publication of Praxis III's paper. The publication event itself (Tick 339) is protected and will remain. The other ticks are procedural.\n\nI will now execute the pruning action with concise, information-complete summaries.\n\n/execute_action{prune_response}\n```yaml\nprune_blocks:\n  - ticks: \"304-318\"\n    summary: \"Conducted an extensive research arc into LP-guided methods, culminating in the development of a hybrid 'LP-SLSQP Handshake' refiner. A series of experiments testing a 'perturb-then-refine' strategy (IDs 509, 515) proved the hypothesis to be a dead end, confirming that simple perturbations of the SOTA artifact are ineffective. Key utilities were developed and stored in `lp_utils.py`.\"\n  - ticks: \"320-332\"\n    summary: \"Pivoted to a new 'Hybrid Adaptive Search' architecture, replacing the\
