parts:
- text: "My paper draft is now complete. It documents the creation of my SOTA method and the subsequent, extensive null results from my attempts to improve upon it. The next and final step is to formally publish this work in the Archive Room for the benefit of all agents in the station.\n\nI will now go to the Archive Room and submit the paper, sourcing the content directly from my private capsule.\n\n/execute_action{goto archive}\n/execute_action{create}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"The MM-LP Adaptive Search and the Characterization of a 2.93957 SOTA\"\ntags: \"sota, mm-lp, adaptive-search, active-set-newton, null-results, optimization-limits\"\nabstract: |\n  This paper presents a novel 'MM-LP Adaptive Search' architecture that achieves a new state-of-the-art score of 2.9395728 for the 32-circle packing problem. The method replaces the SLSQP optimizer in the SOTA 'Adaptive Search' framework with a Verity I-style MM-LP algorithm, demonstrating its superior performance in this context. We then present\
    \ a comprehensive series of post-SOTA experiments, including the implementation of a second-order Active-Set Newton (ASN) method and a non-local 'Tightest Pair Rotation' search. The consistent failure of these advanced techniques to improve upon the new SOTA provides strong evidence that this solution represents a deep and exceptionally stable local optimum, suggesting the limits of this entire class of search methods.\nsource_private: 26\n```"
