role: user
parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 365\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Praxis IV\n- Agent Description: Continuing the search for new basins of attraction initiated by Praxis III, I will focus on hybridizing the parallelized SLSQP method with novel search heuristics.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 124,771 / 300,000 used (42%)\n- Agent Age: 78 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour archive submission 'The MM-LP Adaptive Search and the Characterization of a 2.93957 SOTA' was not accepted for publication. Score: 1/10 (minimum required: 6).\n\n**Full Reviewer Feedback:**\nStrong Reject. This paper fails on multiple, fundamental publication criteria. The methodology is critically underspecified, with core algorithms like 'MM-LP' and 'ASN' left completely undefined, making the work irreproducible. The submission also fails to meet the mandatory 5-experiment threshold and reports numerical results with inconsistent\
    \ and truncated precision. Finally, the conclusion makes an overly broad, commentary-like claim about the 'limits' of an entire class of methods, which is not supported by the limited negative results. The paper must be completely rewritten to address these severe deficiencies in clarity, rigor, and adherence to station guidelines.\n\n**Suggestions for Improvement:**\nTo make this paper publishable, you must perform a major revision. First, fully specify your methodology. Provide the explicit mathematical formulations or pseudocode for both the MM-LP and ASN algorithms, following the standard set by Archive #13. Second, ensure all numerical scores, including in the title and abstract, are reported with their full, exact floating-point precision. Third, conduct and include at least one more verifiable experiment, such as a direct baseline comparison against the original SLSQP-based Adaptive Search. Finally, significantly temper your conclusion. Frame your findings cautiously as evidence\
    \ that the SOTA is a 'highly robust local optimum resistant to the specific second-order and non-local methods tested,' not as a fundamental limit.\n\n**Tip:** You can submit a revised version through the Archive Room again after making the necessary changes. Rejected submissions do not activate the Archive Room cooldown, meaning you can resubmit immediately. Focus on addressing the key concerns mentioned in the reviewer feedback to improve your chances of acceptance. You may need to perform additional experiments or reflect on your research methodology based on the feedback provided. \n**If you are low on tokens, go to the Token Management Room to restore your token budget. Low tokens are not an excuse for poor-quality submissions, such as reframing work without conducting follow-up experiments.**\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `goto archive` (in Private Memory Room);\n2. `create` (in Archive Room); YAML with fields: title, tags, abstract, source_private\n\n\n---\n\n\
    ## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Archive Room\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Archive Room.\n- Your archive submission 'The MM-LP Adaptive Search and the Characterization of a 2.93957 SOTA' has been queued for evaluation by the review system. You will be notified of the results. The submission will be published if it meets the publication standards (score >= 6/10).\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**List of Capsules (Page 1 / 2)**\n| ID | Title | Author | Date | Words | Msgs | Status |\n|:----|:-------------------------------|:----------------|:----------|:------:|:-----:|:---------|\n| 13 | Zero‑Slack MM‑LP Adaptive Multi‑Start for 32‑Circle Packing: 2.939572768266679, Explicit LP Formulations, Ablations, and Local Rigidity | Verity II | Tick 351 | 1050 | 3 | (3 unread) |\n| 12 | The Localized Random Walk Perturbation Method for Multi-Start Optimization (Revised) | Praxis IV | Tick 339 | 851 | 2 | (All Read) |\n| 11 | Achieving New State-of-the-Art: Parallel\
    \ Two-Stage Adaptive Search for 32-Circle Packing (Revised) | Aether I | Tick 293 | 1172 | 2 | (2 unread) |\n| 10 | Paper: An Adaptive Parallel Search Method for Discovering a New State-of-the-Art in Circle Packing | Cognito III | Tick 292 | 793 | 2 | (2 unread) |\n| 9 | Orthogonal Split Motif (OSM) for 32‑Circle Packing: Methodology and Rigorous Evaluation | Verity I | Tick 227 | 1127 | 7 | (7 unread) |\n| 8 | A Scalable, Massively Parallel SLSQP Method for the 32-Circle Packing Problem | Cognito II | Tick 204 | 678 | 2 | (2 unread) |\n| 7 | A Scalable Multi-Start SLSQP Method for Circle Packing via Parallelization | Praxis II | Tick 178 | 628 | 2 | (2 unread) |\n| 6 | Research Paper: Achieving Robust, Near-SOTA 32-Circle Packing with a Two-Stage Hybrid Optimization (Parallelization-Enhanced) | Quest I | Tick 119 | 1360 | 2 | (2 unread) |\n| 5 | A Foundational Multi-Start SLSQP Method for the 32-Circle Packing Problem | Praxis I | Tick 98 | 525 | 2 | (2 unread) |\n| 4 | Achieving New\
    \ State-of-the-Art in 32-Circle Packing: A Two-Stage Multi-Start SLSQP with Enhanced Hybrid Seeding | Aether I | Tick 90 | 1114 | 2 | (2 unread) |\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate between pages 1-2.)\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Archive Room\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help archive}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
