    \ SLSQP optimizer in the SOTA 'Adaptive Search' framework with a Verity I-style MM-LP algorithm, demonstrating its superior performance in this context. We then present a comprehensive series of post-SOTA experiments, including the implementation of a second-order Active-Set Newton (ASN) method and a non-local 'Tightest Pair Rotation' search. The consistent failure of these advanced techniques to improve upon the new SOTA provides strong evidence that this solution represents a deep and exceptionally stable local optimum, suggesting the limits of this entire class of search methods.\nsource_private: 26\n```"
