role: model
parts:
- text: "My reflection is complete. I have a clear, novel, and well-motivated research plan to test the \"Stochastic Motif Jiggle\" hypothesis. The experiment, a three-stage \"Adaptive Jiggle & Refine\" search, is designed to be the ultimate test of the current SOTA's stability.\n\nI will now proceed to the Research Counter to implement this final, self-contained experiment.\n\n/execute_action{goto research}\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Hybrid Non-Local Search: Adaptive Jiggle & Refine\"\ntags: \"non-local-search, stochastic, motif, asn, mm-lp, hybrid-search\"\nabstract: |\n  This submission tests a novel, hybrid, non-local search paradigm designed to escape the deep local optimum of the current SOTA. The 'Adaptive Jiggle & Refine' architecture consists of three stages: (1) a standard MM-LP prospecting stage to find 32 elite candidates, (2) a new 'jiggle' stage where the top 3 tightest pairs of each elite are given a small, seeded, random rotation, and (3) a deep refinement\
    \ of all 32 'jiggled' configurations using a powerful MM-LP+ASN engine. This method synthesizes the stochasticity of LRW, the structural awareness of motif-based moves, and the power of second-order optimization to test the SOTA's rigidity.\ncontent: |\n  import numpy as np\n  from scipy.optimize import linprog\n  from multiprocessing import Pool, cpu_count\n\n  # --- Canonical LP Solver and ASN Components (Self-Contained) ---\n  def solve_radii_lp_with_duals(centers):\n      N_CIRCLES = centers.shape[0]; c = -np.ones(N_CIRCLES)\n      num_b = 4*N_CIRCLES; A_b = np.zeros((num_b, N_CIRCLES)); b_b = np.zeros(num_b)\n      for i in range(N_CIRCLES):\n          A_b[4*i,i]=1; b_b[4*i]=centers[i,0]; A_b[4*i+1,i]=1; b_b[4*i+1]=1-centers[i,0]\n          A_b[4*i+2,i]=1; b_b[4*i+2]=centers[i,1]; A_b[4*i+3,i]=1; b_b[4*i+3]=1-centers[i,1]\n      I, J = np.triu_indices(N_CIRCLES, k=1); num_p = len(I)\n      A_p = np.zeros((num_p, N_CIRCLES)); A_p[np.arange(num_p), I]=1; A_p[np.arange(num_p), J]=1\n\
    \      b_p = np.linalg.norm(centers[I] - centers[J], axis=1)\n      res = linprog(c, A_ub=np.vstack([A_b, A_p]), b_ub=np.concatenate([b_b, b_p]), bounds=(0,None), method='highs')\n      if not res.success: return None\n      return {\"radii\": res.x, \"duals_boundary\": res.ineqlin.marginals[:num_b], \"duals_pairwise\": res.ineqlin.marginals[num_b:], \n              \"slack_boundary\": res.slack[:num_b], \"slack_pairwise\": res.slack[num_b:], \"pairwise_indices\": (I, J)}\n\n  def get_active_set_data(centers, slack_threshold=1e-7):\n      lp_data = solve_radii_lp_with_duals(centers)\n      if lp_data is None: return None\n      lp_data['active_boundary'] = [{'c':i//4, 'f':i%4, 'd':lp_data[\"duals_boundary\"][i]} for i,s in enumerate(lp_data[\"slack_boundary\"]) if s<slack_threshold]\n      I, J = lp_data[\"pairwise_indices\"]\n      lp_data['active_pairwise'] = [{'p':(I[k],J[k]), 'd':lp_data[\"duals_pairwise\"][k]} for k,s in enumerate(lp_data[\"slack_pairwise\"]) if s<slack_threshold]\n\
    \      return lp_data\n\n  def assemble_newton_system(centers, active_set_data):\n      N = centers.shape[0]; g=np.zeros(2*N); H=np.zeros((2*N,2*N))\n      for con in active_set_data['active_boundary']: i,f,d=con['c'],con['f'],con['d']; v=np.array([[-1,0],[1,0],[0,-1],[0,1]])[f]; g[2*i:2*i+2]+=d*v\n      for con in active_set_data['active_pairwise']:\n          i,j=con['p']; d=con['d']; diff=centers[i]-centers[j]; dist=np.linalg.norm(diff)\n          if dist<1e-9: continue\n          u=diff/dist; g[2*i:2*i+2]-=d*u; g[2*j:2*j+2]+=d*u\n          curve=(d/dist)*(np.eye(2)-np.outer(u,u)); H[2*i:2*i+2,2*i:2*i+2]+=curve; H[2*j:2*j+2,2*j:2*j+2]+=curve\n          H[2*i:2*i+2,2*j:2*j+2]-=curve; H[2*j:2*j+2,2*i:2*i+2]-=curve\n      return g, H\n\n  def compute_newton_step(H, g, regularization=1e-8, step_size=1e-4):\n      H_reg=H+regularization*np.eye(H.shape[0])\n      try: dx_raw=np.linalg.solve(H_reg,-g); norm=np.linalg.norm(dx_raw)\n      except np.linalg.LinAlgError: return None\n      if\
    \ norm<1e-9: return None\n      return dx_raw/norm*step_size\n\n  # --- Search Stages ---\n  def mm_lp_optimize(C_start, iters, delta0=0.015):\n      best_C=C_start.copy(); radii=solve_radii_lp_with_duals(best_C)[\"radii\"]; score_best=np.sum(radii)\n      delta,C_anchor=delta0,C_start.copy()\n      for _ in range(iters):\n          n=C_anchor.shape[0]; I,J=np.triu_indices(n,k=1); V0,d0=C_anchor[I]-C_anchor[J],np.linalg.norm(C_anchor[I]-C_anchor[J],axis=1)\n          d0=np.maximum(d0,1e-9); U=(V0.T/d0).T; ux,uy=U[:,0],U[:,1]; x0,y0=C_anchor[:,0],C_anchor[:,1]\n          rows,cols=4*n+len(I),3*n; A_ub,b_ub=np.zeros((rows,cols)),np.zeros(rows); r,x,y=range(n),range(n,2*n),range(2*n,3*n); row=0\n          for i in range(n): A_ub[row,r[i]]=1;A_ub[row,x[i]]=-1;row+=1; A_ub[row,r[i]]=1;A_ub[row,x[i]]=1;b_ub[row]=1;row+=1; A_ub[row,r[i]]=1;A_ub[row,y[i]]=-1;row+=1; A_ub[row,r[i]]=1;A_ub[row,y[i]]=1;b_ub[row]=1;row+=1\n          for k in range(len(I)): i,j=I[k],J[k]; A_ub[row,r[i]]=1;A_ub[row,r[j]]=1;\
    \ A_ub[row,x[i]]=-ux[k];A_ub[row,y[i]]=-uy[k];A_ub[row,x[j]]=ux[k];A_ub[row,y[j]]=uy[k]; b_ub[row]=d0[k]-ux[k]*x0[i]-uy[k]*y0[i]+ux[k]*x0[j]+uy[k]*y0[j]; row+=1\n          c=np.zeros(cols); c[:n]=-1; bounds=[(0,.5)]*n+[(max(1e-6,x0[i]-delta),min(1-1e-6,x0[i]+delta)) for i in range(n)]+[(max(1e-6,y0[i]-delta),min(1-1e-6,y0[i]+delta)) for i in range(n)]\n          res=linprog(c,A_ub,b_ub,bounds=bounds,method=\"highs\");\n          if not res.success: delta*=.6; continue\n          C_lin=np.stack([res.x[n:2*n],res.x[2*n:3*n]],axis=1); radii=solve_radii_lp_with_duals(C_lin)[\"radii\"]; score_exact=np.sum(radii)\n          if score_exact>score_best: best_C,score_best=C_lin.copy(),score_exact; C_anchor=C_lin.copy(); delta=min(.05,1.2*delta)\n          else: delta*=.8\n      final_radii=solve_radii_lp_with_duals(best_C)[\"radii\"]\n      return best_C, final_radii, score_best\n\n  def asn_refine(centers_initial, iters=5):\n      C_best=centers_initial.copy(); score_best=np.sum(solve_radii_lp_with_duals(C_best)[\"\
    radii\"])\n      for _ in range(iters):\n          info=get_active_set_data(C_best);\n          if info is None: break\n          g,H=assemble_newton_system(C_best,info); dx=compute_newton_step(H,g)\n          if dx is None: break\n          alpha, accepted = 1.0, False\n          for _ in range(5):\n              C_try = C_best+alpha*dx.reshape(32,2); radii=solve_radii_lp_with_duals(C_try)[\"radii\"]; score_try=np.sum(radii)\n              if score_try>score_best: C_best,score_best,accepted=C_try,score_try,True; break\n              alpha/=.5\n          if not accepted: break\n      return C_best, solve_radii_lp_with_duals(C_best)[\"radii\"], score_best\n\n  def get_seed(seed): rng=np.random.default_rng(seed); st=seed%3; C=[]; N=32\n      if st==0: grid=np.stack(np.meshgrid(np.linspace(.1,.9,6),np.linspace(.1,.9,6)),-1).reshape(-1,2)[:N]; C=np.clip(grid+(rng.random((N,2))-.5)*.08,.05,.95)\n      elif st==1: pts=[rng.uniform(.1,.9,2)]; [pts.append(cands[np.argmax(np.min(np.sum((cands[:,None,:]-np.array(pts)[None,:,:])**2,-1),1))])\
    \ for _ in range(N-1) for cands in [rng.uniform(.1,.9,(200,2))]]; C=np.array(pts)\n      else: rows=[5,6,5,6,5,5]; y=.95; [C.append([((1-(c-1)*.15)/2)+j*.15,y]) for i,c in enumerate(rows) for j in range(c) if len(C)<N]; y-=.15; C=np.array(C)\n      return C\n  \n  def prospect_worker(args): s,i,d=args; C=get_seed(s); _,_,score=mm_lp_optimize(C,i,d); return score, C\n  def refine_worker(args): C_jiggled, mmlp_i, asn_i=args; C1=mm_lp_optimize(C_jiggled,mmlp_i)[0]; return asn_refine(C1, asn_i)\n  \n  def construct_packing() -> tuple:\n      N_PROSPECT, N_ELITE, K_PAIRS, SIGMA_ANGLE = 1024, 32, 3, 0.01\n      PROSPECT_ITER, REFINE_MMLP_ITER, REFINE_ASN_ITER = 20, 15, 5\n\n      with Pool(cpu_count()) as p: prospect_results = p.map(prospect_worker, [(i,PROSPECT_ITER,.015) for i in range(N_PROSPECT)])\n      prospect_results.sort(key=lambda x:x[0], reverse=True)\n      elite_centers = [res[1] for res in prospect_results[:N_ELITE]]\n\n      jiggled_centers = []\n      for i, centers in enumerate(elite_centers):\n\
    \          np.random.seed(i) # Deterministic jiggle per elite\n          lp_data = solve_radii_lp_with_duals(centers)\n          if lp_data is None: jiggled_centers.append(centers); continue\n          I,J,slacks=lp_data[\"pairwise_indices\"][0],lp_data[\"pairwise_indices\"][1],lp_data[\"slack_pairwise\"]\n          sorted_indices = np.argsort(slacks); top_k_pairs=[(I[k],J[k]) for k in sorted_indices[:K_PAIRS]]\n          \n          C_new = centers.copy()\n          for p_idx1, p_idx2 in top_k_pairs:\n              c1,c2=C_new[p_idx1],C_new[p_idx2]; mid=(c1+c2)/2; v1=c1-mid\n              angle=np.random.normal(0,SIGMA_ANGLE); c,s=np.cos(angle),np.sin(angle); rot=np.array([[c,-s],[s,c]])\n              v1_rot=rot@v1; C_new[p_idx1]=mid+v1_rot; C_new[p_idx2]=mid-v1_rot\n          jiggled_centers.append(np.clip(C_new, 1e-6, 1-1e-6))\n      \n      with Pool(cpu_count()) as p: refine_results = p.map(refine_worker, [(c,REFINE_MMLP_ITER,REFINE_ASN_ITER) for c in jiggled_centers])\n      \n\
    \      best_c, best_r, best_s = None, None, -1.0\n      for c,r,s in refine_results:\n          if s > best_s: best_c,best_r,best_s = c,r,s\n              \n      if best_c is None: return get_seed(0), np.full((32,), .05)\n      return best_c, best_r * (1.0 - 1e-9)\n```"
