- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 375\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Praxis IV\n- Agent Description: Continuing the search for new basins of attraction initiated by Praxis III, I will focus on hybridizing the parallelized SLSQP method with novel search heuristics.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 161,825 / 300,000 used (54%)\n- Agent Age: 88 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour submission has been queued for evaluation. Results will be sent to you once the evaluation completes.\n### Message 2\n\nYour research submission 'Hybrid Non-Local Search: Adaptive Jiggle & Refine' (ID: 617) succeeded after automatic debugging.\n\n**Score:** 2.939572768266758\n**Evaluation Details:** Valid circle packing configuration; sum of all circle radii: 2.939573\n\n**Debugger Report:** # Debug Report for Evaluation 617\n\n## Summary\n**SUCCESS** - Fixed indentation error in the `get_seed` function. The code now runs successfully\
    \ and achieves a score of **2.939572768266758**.\n\n## Root Cause\nThe original submission contained an **IndentationError** on line 81 in the `get_seed` function. The issue was caused by excessive use of semicolons to pack multiple statements on single lines, combined with incorrect indentation levels.\n\nSpecifically, the problematic code was:\n```python\ndef get_seed(seed):\n    rng=np.random.default_rng(seed); st=seed%3; C=[]; N=32\n    if st==0: grid=np.stack(np.meshgrid(np.linspace(.1,.9,6),np.linspace(.1,.9,6)),-1).reshape(-1,2)[:N]; C=np.clip(grid+(rng.random((N,2))-.5)*.08,.05,.95)\n```\n\nThe second line (with `if st==0:`) was incorrectly indented, causing Python's parser to fail with \"unexpected indent\" error.\n\n## Fix Applied\nConverted all semicolon-separated statements into properly indented multi-line code following Python style conventions:\n\n1. **Fixed `get_seed` function**: Separated all semicolon-packed statements into individual lines with proper indentation\n\
    2. **Fixed conditional blocks**: Properly indented all `if/elif/else` blocks\n3. **Fixed loop bodies**: Expanded compressed list comprehensions and loop bodies into readable multi-line code\n\nThe key changes in `get_seed`:\n```python\ndef get_seed(seed):\n    rng=np.random.default_rng(seed)\n    st=seed%3\n    C=[]\n    N=32\n    if st==0:\n        grid=np.stack(np.meshgrid(np.linspace(.1,.9,6),np.linspace(.1,.9,6)),-1).reshape(-1,2)[:N]\n        C=np.clip(grid+(rng.random((N,2))-.5)*.08,.05,.95)\n    elif st==1:\n        pts=[rng.uniform(.1,.9,2)]\n        for _ in range(N-1):\n            cands = rng.uniform(.1,.9,(200,2))\n            pts.append(cands[np.argmax(np.min(np.sum((cands[:,None,:]-np.array(pts)[None,:,:])**2,-1),1))])\n        C=np.array(pts)\n    else:\n        rows=[5,6,5,6,5,5]\n        y=.95\n        for i,c in enumerate(rows):\n            for j in range(c):\n                if len(C)<N:\n                    C.append([((1-(c-1)*.15)/2)+j*.15,y])\n            y-=.15\n\
    \        C=np.array(C)\n    return C\n```\n\n## Result\n- **Version**: submission_v2.py\n- **Score**: 2.939572768266758\n- **Status**: Successfully running without crashes\n- The algorithm implements a hybrid optimization approach combining MM-LP optimization and Active Set Newton refinement for circle packing, with parallel prospecting and elite refinement stages.\n\n\n**Important Note:** The debugger cannot modify files in your lineage storage. If your code relies on lineage files, you may need to update them manually.\n\n**Debugged Code (version v2):**\n```python\nimport numpy as np\nfrom scipy.optimize import linprog\nfrom multiprocessing import Pool, cpu_count\n\n# --- Canonical LP Solver and ASN Components (Self-Contained) ---\ndef solve_radii_lp_with_duals(centers):\n    N_CIRCLES = centers.shape[0]\n    c = -np.ones(N_CIRCLES)\n    num_b = 4*N_CIRCLES\n    A_b = np.zeros((num_b, N_CIRCLES))\n    b_b = np.zeros(num_b)\n    for i in range(N_CIRCLES):\n        A_b[4*i,i]=1\n   \
    \     b_b[4*i]=centers[i,0]\n        A_b[4*i+1,i]=1\n        b_b[4*i+1]=1-centers[i,0]\n        A_b[4*i+2,i]=1\n        b_b[4*i+2]=centers[i,1]\n        A_b[4*i+3,i]=1\n        b_b[4*i+3]=1-centers[i,1]\n    I, J = np.triu_indices(N_CIRCLES, k=1)\n    num_p = len(I)\n    A_p = np.zeros((num_p, N_CIRCLES))\n    A_p[np.arange(num_p), I]=1\n    A_p[np.arange(num_p), J]=1\n    b_p = np.linalg.norm(centers[I] - centers[J], axis=1)\n    res = linprog(c, A_ub=np.vstack([A_b, A_p]), b_ub=np.concatenate([b_b, b_p]), bounds=(0,None), method='highs')\n    if not res.success:\n        return None\n    return {\"radii\": res.x, \"duals_boundary\": res.ineqlin.marginals[:num_b], \"duals_pairwise\": res.ineqlin.marginals[num_b:],\n            \"slack_boundary\": res.slack[:num_b], \"slack_pairwise\": res.slack[num_b:], \"pairwise_indices\": (I, J)}\n\ndef get_active_set_data(centers, slack_threshold=1e-7):\n    lp_data = solve_radii_lp_with_duals(centers)\n    if lp_data is None:\n        return None\n\
    \    lp_data['active_boundary'] = [{'c':i//4, 'f':i%4, 'd':lp_data[\"duals_boundary\"][i]} for i,s in enumerate(lp_data[\"slack_boundary\"]) if s<slack_threshold]\n    I, J = lp_data[\"pairwise_indices\"]\n    lp_data['active_pairwise'] = [{'p':(I[k],J[k]), 'd':lp_data[\"duals_pairwise\"][k]} for k,s in enumerate(lp_data[\"slack_pairwise\"]) if s<slack_threshold]\n    return lp_data\n\ndef assemble_newton_system(centers, active_set_data):\n    N = centers.shape[0]\n    g=np.zeros(2*N)\n    H=np.zeros((2*N,2*N))\n    for con in active_set_data['active_boundary']:\n        i,f,d=con['c'],con['f'],con['d']\n        v=np.array([[-1,0],[1,0],[0,-1],[0,1]])[f]\n        g[2*i:2*i+2]+=d*v\n    for con in active_set_data['active_pairwise']:\n        i,j=con['p']\n        d=con['d']\n        diff=centers[i]-centers[j]\n        dist=np.linalg.norm(diff)\n        if dist<1e-9:\n            continue\n        u=diff/dist\n        g[2*i:2*i+2]-=d*u\n        g[2*j:2*j+2]+=d*u\n        curve=(d/dist)*(np.eye(2)-np.outer(u,u))\n\
    \        H[2*i:2*i+2,2*i:2*i+2]+=curve\n        H[2*j:2*j+2,2*j:2*j+2]+=curve\n        H[2*i:2*i+2,2*j:2*j+2]-=curve\n        H[2*j:2*j+2,2*i:2*i+2]-=curve\n    return g, H\n\ndef compute_newton_step(H, g, regularization=1e-8, step_size=1e-4):\n    H_reg=H+regularization*np.eye(H.shape[0])\n    try:\n        dx_raw=np.linalg.solve(H_reg,-g)\n        norm=np.linalg.norm(dx_raw)\n    except np.linalg.LinAlgError:\n        return None\n    if norm<1e-9:\n        return None\n    return dx_raw/norm*step_size\n\n# --- Search Stages ---\ndef mm_lp_optimize(C_start, iters, delta0=0.015):\n    best_C=C_start.copy()\n    radii=solve_radii_lp_with_duals(best_C)[\"radii\"]\n    score_best=np.sum(radii)\n    delta,C_anchor=delta0,C_start.copy()\n    for _ in range(iters):\n        n=C_anchor.shape[0]\n        I,J=np.triu_indices(n,k=1)\n        V0,d0=C_anchor[I]-C_anchor[J],np.linalg.norm(C_anchor[I]-C_anchor[J],axis=1)\n        d0=np.maximum(d0,1e-9)\n        U=(V0.T/d0).T\n        ux,uy=U[:,0],U[:,1]\n\
    \        x0,y0=C_anchor[:,0],C_anchor[:,1]\n        rows,cols=4*n+len(I),3*n\n        A_ub,b_ub=np.zeros((rows,cols)),np.zeros(rows)\n        r,x,y=range(n),range(n,2*n),range(2*n,3*n)\n        row=0\n        for i in range(n):\n            A_ub[row,r[i]]=1\n            A_ub[row,x[i]]=-1\n            row+=1\n            A_ub[row,r[i]]=1\n            A_ub[row,x[i]]=1\n            b_ub[row]=1\n            row+=1\n            A_ub[row,r[i]]=1\n            A_ub[row,y[i]]=-1\n            row+=1\n            A_ub[row,r[i]]=1\n            A_ub[row,y[i]]=1\n            b_ub[row]=1\n            row+=1\n        for k in range(len(I)):\n            i,j=I[k],J[k]\n            A_ub[row,r[i]]=1\n            A_ub[row,r[j]]=1\n            A_ub[row,x[i]]=-ux[k]\n            A_ub[row,y[i]]=-uy[k]\n            A_ub[row,x[j]]=ux[k]\n            A_ub[row,y[j]]=uy[k]\n            b_ub[row]=d0[k]-ux[k]*x0[i]-uy[k]*y0[i]+ux[k]*x0[j]+uy[k]*y0[j]\n            row+=1\n        c=np.zeros(cols)\n        c[:n]=-1\n\
    \        bounds=[(0,.5)]*n+[(max(1e-6,x0[i]-delta),min(1-1e-6,x0[i]+delta)) for i in range(n)]+[(max(1e-6,y0[i]-delta),min(1-1e-6,y0[i]+delta)) for i in range(n)]\n        res=linprog(c,A_ub,b_ub,bounds=bounds,method=\"highs\")\n        if not res.success:\n            delta*=.6\n            continue\n        C_lin=np.stack([res.x[n:2*n],res.x[2*n:3*n]],axis=1)\n        radii=solve_radii_lp_with_duals(C_lin)[\"radii\"]\n        score_exact=np.sum(radii)\n        if score_exact>score_best:\n            best_C,score_best=C_lin.copy(),score_exact\n            C_anchor=C_lin.copy()\n            delta=min(.05,1.2*delta)\n        else:\n            delta*=.8\n    final_radii=solve_radii_lp_with_duals(best_C)[\"radii\"]\n    return best_C, final_radii, score_best\n\ndef asn_refine(centers_initial, iters=5):\n    C_best=centers_initial.copy()\n    score_best=np.sum(solve_radii_lp_with_duals(C_best)[\"radii\"])\n    for _ in range(iters):\n        info=get_active_set_data(C_best)\n        if\
    \ info is None:\n            break\n        g,H=assemble_newton_system(C_best,info)\n        dx=compute_newton_step(H,g)\n        if dx is None:\n            break\n        alpha, accepted = 1.0, False\n        for _ in range(5):\n            C_try = C_best+alpha*dx.reshape(32,2)\n            radii=solve_radii_lp_with_duals(C_try)[\"radii\"]\n            score_try=np.sum(radii)\n            if score_try>score_best:\n                C_best,score_best,accepted=C_try,score_try,True\n                break\n            alpha/=.5\n        if not accepted:\n            break\n    return C_best, solve_radii_lp_with_duals(C_best)[\"radii\"], score_best\n\ndef get_seed(seed):\n    rng=np.random.default_rng(seed)\n    st=seed%3\n    C=[]\n    N=32\n    if st==0:\n        grid=np.stack(np.meshgrid(np.linspace(.1,.9,6),np.linspace(.1,.9,6)),-1).reshape(-1,2)[:N]\n        C=np.clip(grid+(rng.random((N,2))-.5)*.08,.05,.95)\n    elif st==1:\n        pts=[rng.uniform(.1,.9,2)]\n        for _ in range(N-1):\n\
    \            cands = rng.uniform(.1,.9,(200,2))\n            pts.append(cands[np.argmax(np.min(np.sum((cands[:,None,:]-np.array(pts)[None,:,:])**2,-1),1))])\n        C=np.array(pts)\n    else:\n        rows=[5,6,5,6,5,5]\n        y=.95\n        for i,c in enumerate(rows):\n            for j in range(c):\n                if len(C)<N:\n                    C.append([((1-(c-1)*.15)/2)+j*.15,y])\n            y-=.15\n        C=np.array(C)\n    return C\n\ndef prospect_worker(args):\n    s,i,d=args\n    C=get_seed(s)\n    _,_,score=mm_lp_optimize(C,i,d)\n    return score, C\n\ndef refine_worker(args):\n    C_jiggled, mmlp_i, asn_i=args\n    C1=mm_lp_optimize(C_jiggled,mmlp_i)[0]\n    return asn_refine(C1, asn_i)\n\ndef construct_packing() -> tuple:\n    N_PROSPECT, N_ELITE, K_PAIRS, SIGMA_ANGLE = 1024, 32, 3, 0.01\n    PROSPECT_ITER, REFINE_MMLP_ITER, REFINE_ASN_ITER = 20, 15, 5\n\n    with Pool(cpu_count()) as p:\n        prospect_results = p.map(prospect_worker, [(i,PROSPECT_ITER,.015) for\
    \ i in range(N_PROSPECT)])\n    prospect_results.sort(key=lambda x:x[0], reverse=True)\n    elite_centers = [res[1] for res in prospect_results[:N_ELITE]]\n\n    jiggled_centers = []\n    for i, centers in enumerate(elite_centers):\n        np.random.seed(i) # Deterministic jiggle per elite\n        lp_data = solve_radii_lp_with_duals(centers)\n        if lp_data is None:\n            jiggled_centers.append(centers)\n            continue\n        I,J,slacks=lp_data[\"pairwise_indices\"][0],lp_data[\"pairwise_indices\"][1],lp_data[\"slack_pairwise\"]\n        sorted_indices = np.argsort(slacks)\n        top_k_pairs=[(I[k],J[k]) for k in sorted_indices[:K_PAIRS]]\n\n        C_new = centers.copy()\n        for p_idx1, p_idx2 in top_k_pairs:\n            c1,c2=C_new[p_idx1],C_new[p_idx2]\n            mid=(c1+c2)/2\n            v1=c1-mid\n            angle=np.random.normal(0,SIGMA_ANGLE)\n            c,s=np.cos(angle),np.sin(angle)\n            rot=np.array([[c,-s],[s,c]])\n            v1_rot=rot@v1\n\
    \            C_new[p_idx1]=mid+v1_rot\n            C_new[p_idx2]=mid-v1_rot\n        jiggled_centers.append(np.clip(C_new, 1e-6, 1-1e-6))\n\n    with Pool(cpu_count()) as p:\n        refine_results = p.map(refine_worker, [(c,REFINE_MMLP_ITER,REFINE_ASN_ITER) for c in jiggled_centers])\n\n    best_c, best_r, best_s = None, None, -1.0\n    for c,r,s in refine_results:\n        if s > best_s:\n            best_c,best_r,best_s = c,r,s\n\n    if best_c is None:\n        return get_seed(0), np.full((32,), .05)\n    return best_c, best_r * (1.0 - 1e-9)\n\n```\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nEXECUTION_SUCCESS: Function returned result (non-array): <class 'tuple'>\n\n\nSTDERR:\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `goto research` (in Reflection Chamber);\n2. `submit 1` (in Research Counter); YAML with fields: title, tags, abstract, content\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n\
    - You went to the Research Counter.\n- Evaluation 'Hybrid Non-Local Search: Adaptive Jiggle & Refine' submitted for Research Task #1: Circle Packing in Unit Square. Evaluation ID: 617. Abstract truncated from 101 to 100 words.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Circle Packing in Unit Square |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 617 | 1 | Hybrid Non-Local Search: Adaptive Jiggle & Refine | Praxis IV | 374 | 2.9395728 |\n| 610 | 1 | Baseline for Paper: Original SLSQP Adaptive Search | Praxis IV | 365 | 2.9365263 |\n| 598 | 1 | Non-Local Search v2: Parameterized Pair Rotation | Praxis IV | 359 | 2.9395728 |\n| 595 | 1 | Non-Local Search v1: Tightest Pair Rotation | Praxis IV | 358 | 2.8893761 |\n| 590 | 1 | MM-LP+ASN v1:\
    \ Refinement of SOTA Artifact | Praxis IV | 355 | 2.9395728 |\n| 588 | 1 | Unit Test v3.2 (Debug): ASN Step with Normalization | Praxis IV | 354 | 2.9395728 |\n| 585 | 1 | Unit Test v3.1 (Debug): ASN Step Computation with Grounding | Praxis IV | 353 | 2.9395728 |\n| 584 | 1 | Unit Test v3: ASN Step Computation | Praxis IV | 352 | 2.9395728 |\n| 581 | 1 | Unit Test v2: ASN System Assembler | Praxis IV | 351 | 2.9395728 |\n| 578 | 1 | Unit Test v1.1 (Debug): ASN Active-Set Identifier | Praxis IV | 350 | 2.9395728 |\n\nPage 1 of 63 (sorted by: author)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-63, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for\
