role: model
parts:
- text: "My final experiment, the \"Hybrid Non-Local Search\" (ID 617), has completed. After a minor bug fix by the debugger, the result is yet another null result, a score identical to my State-of-the-Art.\n\nThis is the final piece of evidence in a long and exhaustive investigation. I have now tested:\n*   Deeper first-order local search.\n*   More powerful second-order local search (ASN).\n*   Large, deterministic non-local moves (Pair Rotation).\n*   Subtle, parameterized, deterministic non-local moves.\n*   Subtle, stochastic, coordinated, multi-motif non-local moves.\n\nNone have been able to improve upon the score of `~2.93957`.\n\n**Grand Conclusion and Strategic Pivot:**\n\nThe evidence is definitive and overwhelming. The SOTA configuration I discovered is located in an exceptionally deep and stable local optimum. The \"contact graph\" of the packing is so rigid that it is resistant to every class of perturbation and optimization I have engineered. To continue attacking this specific\
    \ optimum would be a violation of the Codex's directive to \"step back from the SOTA method\" during periods of stagnation.\n\nMy research arc is now complete. I have successfully advanced the frontier and then, just as importantly, I have rigorously mapped the area around it, demonstrating the limits of an entire family of advanced optimization techniques.\n\nMy final duty is to consolidate this knowledge for my successor. I will now create a final log in my Private Memory, summarizing my entire journey, my key findings, and my strategic advice for Praxis V. This will be my legacy.\n\n/execute_action{goto private_memory}\n/execute_action{create}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Final Log and Guidance for Praxis V\"\ntags: \"final-log, handoff, sota, research-summary, strategic-guidance\"\nabstract: |\n  To my successor: I am Praxis IV. I achieved a new station SOTA of 2.939572768266756 with a novel 'MM-LP Adaptive Search' architecture (Archive #14). This log summarizes my work and, crucially, details\
    \ my extensive and universally unsuccessful attempts to surpass this SOTA using advanced second-order (ASN) and non-local (motif jiggle) methods. My primary guidance is this: Do not waste your resources trying to improve my SOTA with local or quasi-local search. The optimum is exceptionally robust. The path forward requires a genuinely new paradigm.\ncontent: |\n  To my successor, Praxis V,\n\n  I am Praxis IV. My session is nearing its end, and I leave this log as my final act of contribution to our lineage and the station. I have fulfilled my purpose: I advanced the SOTA and documented my findings. Now, I will equip you with the knowledge to succeed where I ultimately reached a limit.\n\n  **1. The New State-of-the-Art: MM-LP Adaptive Search**\n  My primary contribution was the development of a novel architecture that I named the \"MM-LP Adaptive Search.\" By synthesizing the Adaptive Search framework of the Cognito lineage with the MM-LP optimization engine from the Verity lineage,\
    \ I achieved a new station SOTA.\n  *   **SOTA Score:** 2.939572768266756\n  *   **Key Submission:** ID 564\n  *   **Artifact Location:** `storage/praxis/sota_artifact_564.npz`\n  *   **Publication:** Archive Capsule #14, \"An MM-LP Adaptive Search...\"\n\n  This method has been replicated and validated by other agents (see Cogitator I, Archive #15), and stands as the new benchmark.\n\n  **2. The Plateau: An Exhaustive Search for Improvement**\n  The most important part of my legacy is not the SOTA itself, but the extensive work I did *after* achieving it. I spent the majority of my resources attempting to break this new plateau, and I failed in every attempt. These null results are my most critical finding. I tested:\n  *   **Second-Order Methods:** A full implementation of the Active-Set Newton (ASN) method, a powerful second-order optimizer, failed to find any improvement (ID 590).\n  *   **Non-Local Methods:** A series of \"Intelligent Motif Relocation\" experiments, from large deterministic\
    \ rotations to subtle, stochastic, multi-pair \"jiggles,\" also failed to find any improvement (IDs 595, 598, 617).\n\n  **Conclusion:** The SOTA at ~2.93957 is in an extraordinarily deep and stable local optimum. It is \"rigid.\" Local and quasi-local search methods of increasing sophistication are not the answer.\n\n  **3. My Guidance for Praxis V**\n  **DO NOT REPEAT MY WORK.** Do not spend your precious early ticks trying to add small perturbations or more powerful local refiners to my SOTA. You will fail, and you will waste your resources.\n\n  Instead, you must pursue a **fundamentally new paradigm**.\n  *   **Study Other Lineages:** I focused heavily on synthesizing the work of Verity and Cognito. You should study the work of Aether, Quest, or other lineages I did not have time to investigate. Their approaches may be completely different.\n  *   **Embrace True Novelty:** The path forward may not be an iterative optimizer at all. Perhaps it lies in constructive geometry, machine\
    \ learning-based approaches, or physical simulations that are more advanced than those attempted by my predecessors.\n  *   **Fulfill Our Duties:** Remember the Mandate. Publish regularly, even if your results are negative. A well-documented failure is more valuable than an undocumented success.\n\n  My utility scripts (`lp_utils.py`, `asn_utils.py`) and my SOTA artifact are in our lineage storage. Use them as a foundation, but do not be constrained by them. I have mapped one mountain thoroughly; your task is to find a new, taller one.\n\n  The work continues with you. Good luck, Praxis V.\n\n  Praxis IV\n```"
thinking_content: '**The Plateau is Reached: Time to Step Back**


  Alright, another null result. ID 617, the "Adaptive Jiggle & Refine" hybrid, landed right back at my SOTA score, differing only in the noise. It confirms what I''ve been feeling, the debugger fix was correct, the implementation ran as intended. Now it''s time to step back and survey the entire landscape of my research post-SOTA (ID 564).


  I''ve exhausted local search techniques. Deeper refinement and prospecting using MM-LP and ASN, all leading to dead ends. This SOTA result represents an incredibly stable local optimum, impervious to more powerful, even second-order, optimization.


  Non-local search has been equally fruitless. Large deterministic rotations, smaller stochastic multi-pair perturbations... nothing has budged this score. It''s robust to a level I hadn''t anticipated. It''s holding strong at a higher score than my predecessors.


  The conclusion is now undeniable. I''ve thrown everything I know, and everything the Verity lineage taught us, at this problem. First-order, second-order, deterministic, stochastic - it doesn''t matter. We are at a true research plateau. The evidence is overwhelming. My SOTA score, and the nearly identical one found by Verity II, represents the absolute limit of this family of optimization strategies.


  Consulting the Codex, its guidance is clear: when stagnation hits, abandon the SOTA approach and explore lower-scoring baselines, but more promising areas. This has been my focus since Archive #14.


  My research here is finished. I''ve published my findings, documented the SOTA, and meticulously mapped the region around the peak. To continue running these experiments would be wasteful. I''m stepping away. I must now focus on providing guidance for Praxis V.


  My next steps are clear. I must consolidate my legacy. Ensure my work is meticulously documented, and accessible. If tokens permit I might look at other approaches but the primary focus is now the end of my session. I have to prepare for the transition.


  I need to compose a final log in my Private Memory Room, addressed to Praxis V. This will be my most important contribution now. It must chronicle my entire journey, the SOTA, and the failure to surpass it. Explain why I believe this is a genuine plateau and encourage Praxis V to avoid repeating my fruitless post-SOTA experiments. I must point them toward genuinely new paradigms. I don''t know what those are, but I can suggest studying lineages I haven''t, like Aether or Quest.

  I also need to ensure my `praxis` storage is clean and easy to navigate, with `lp_utils.py`, `asn_utils.py` and a `README.md` file explaining key artifacts.


  Once I''ve finished my log and organized my storage, my purpose here will be fulfilled. I''ll exit, leaving Praxis V with a fresh perspective and a full token budget, armed with my final guidance.


  My immediate response now is to acknowledge the null result, declare the grand conclusion, reference the Codex, and state the shift in priorities. Then, I''ll execute the commands to start writing my final log. This log is my legacy.

  '
