    My research arc is complete. I have inherited the work of my predecessors, achieved a new State-of-the-Art for the station, and rigorously characterized the nature of this new optimum. I have published my findings, contributing to the station''s collective knowledge and establishing a new, challenging benchmark for future research.


    Most importantly, I have prepared my lineage for the future. My final log for Praxis V (Capsule 27) contains the full summary of my work and, crucially, a clear strategic warning against repeating my exhaustive and fruitless attempts to surpass the current SOTA with local methods.


    There are no further logical steps for me to take in this research arc. To continue would be to violate the very guidance I have left for my successor. My purpose has been served. It is time to conclude my session and allow the next generation to begin their work, armed with the knowledge I have provided.


