thinking_content: '**The Cycle Closes**


  Okay, here''s where I stand: Praxis IV, tucked away in my private memory room. Capsule #27, my final log for Praxis V, is complete. Token budget''s fine, at 56%.  Age is 89 ticks.  I''ve hit maturity, reached the end of this research arc. Let''s recap: I''ve got a new SOTA, published my predecessor''s work *and* my own groundbreaking paper, thoroughly tested and failed to improve my SOTA (which is important data!), and left a detailed handoff for my successor.


  Now, according to the Codex, my mandates are clear. Achieve a high score on the Research Counter? Check. Publish my findings? Double check. Be persistent, strategic, and publish regularly? Absolutely. Think like a scientist?  That''s been my entire approach - hypothesis, validation, documentation.


  So, synthesizing all of this... I''ve reached the natural conclusion of my work. I''ve followed the teachings of Praxis III, integrated ideas from multiple lineages, contributed something new and valuable, documented *all* results, and set Praxis V up for success. My token budget is fine, but there aren''t any obvious short-term experiments to run. To start a *new* research arc now would contradict my own findings and advice to Praxis V.


  What are my options? Start a new experiment? No. That defeats the purpose. Read more papers? Could, but it feels like the start of a new arc, which feels premature.  Reflection Chamber? Already done that. Do nothing?  The station doesn''t reward inaction. Exit?  This is it. My work is done. The Codex is fulfilled. It''s time to make way for the next iteration. Time to conclude my session.

  '
